1
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:52,803
(AIRCRAFT DRONING)

2
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:59,143
(SIREN WAILING)

3
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:03,648
(SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

4
00:01:06,108 --> 00:01:07,652
(PEOPLE CLAMORING)

5
00:01:10,655 --> 00:01:12,198
(CONTINUES SHOUTING)
(TOLLING)

6
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:17,119
(CLAMORING CONTINUES)

7
00:01:17,203 --> 00:01:18,746
(GUARD SHOUTING)

8
00:01:28,714 --> 00:01:30,841
(CAR ENGINE REVVING)

9
00:01:32,343 --> 00:01:34,095
(SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

10
00:01:47,817 --> 00:01:49,235
(PANTING)

11
00:01:50,027 --> 00:01:50,611
PRISONER 1:
Where are you going?

12
00:01:51,946 --> 00:01:53,281
PRISONER 2: Help me!

13
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:54,949
PRISONER 3: Over here!

14
00:01:55,032 --> 00:01:56,284
(PRISONERS CONTINUE SHOUTING)

15
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:59,704
(SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

16
00:02:21,017 --> 00:02:22,101
(GRUNTING)

17
00:02:27,648 --> 00:02:28,899
Go!

18
00:02:29,317 --> 00:02:30,318
Go!

19
00:02:30,985 --> 00:02:34,530
That was a B-29, bub.
There's no outrunning
what's coming.

20
00:02:35,197 --> 00:02:36,574
OFFICER: Yashida!

21
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:38,534
(SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

22
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:44,165
You're better
off down here.

23
00:02:45,082 --> 00:02:46,834
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

24
00:02:46,917 --> 00:02:48,669
I'd hurry
if I were you.

25
00:02:48,753 --> 00:02:50,046
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

26
00:03:13,277 --> 00:03:14,570
(BLADE UNSHEATHES)

27
00:03:16,947 --> 00:03:18,240
(GROANS)

28
00:03:20,034 --> 00:03:21,702
(BOTH GROANING)

29
00:03:37,009 --> 00:03:38,052
(GASPS)

30
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:39,470
(HIGH-PITCHED WHINING)

31
00:03:53,984 --> 00:03:54,985
Run. Now!

32
00:04:04,328 --> 00:04:05,496
(YASHIDA SHOUTS)

33
00:04:06,372 --> 00:04:07,957
Stay down!

34
00:04:15,339 --> 00:04:16,757
(STRAINING)

35
00:04:21,512 --> 00:04:22,721
(LOGAN GRUNTS)

36
00:04:34,275 --> 00:04:35,693
(GASPING)

37
00:04:36,944 --> 00:04:38,404
(WHEEZING)

38
00:04:40,406 --> 00:04:41,615
(GRUNTING)

39
00:04:45,703 --> 00:04:47,288
(GROANS LOUDLY)

40
00:04:54,587 --> 00:04:56,797
No, wait!
No, no. Wait.

41
00:04:59,717 --> 00:05:02,303
No. It's not safe.

42
00:05:04,138 --> 00:05:08,142
JEAN GREY: Wake up, wake up,
wake up. Wake up.
(PANTING)

43
00:05:09,393 --> 00:05:11,312
Where were you?

44
00:05:14,064 --> 00:05:15,357
Nagasaki.

45
00:05:16,484 --> 00:05:18,694
That far back?

46
00:05:25,409 --> 00:05:26,452
(KISSES)

47
00:05:26,535 --> 00:05:27,661
You're here.

48
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:28,913
Of course.

49
00:05:29,079 --> 00:05:30,873
Can you stay?

50
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:33,626
You know I can't.

51
00:05:34,627 --> 00:05:36,795
Jean, I'm so sorry.

52
00:05:37,213 --> 00:05:38,214
I know.

53
00:05:38,339 --> 00:05:42,009
I'll never hurt you
or anyone ever again.

54
00:05:42,176 --> 00:05:43,469
I made a vow.

55
00:05:44,261 --> 00:05:46,055
A solemn vow?

56
00:05:46,388 --> 00:05:48,390
You're making fun of me.

57
00:05:50,309 --> 00:05:52,478
It's too late.

58
00:05:57,608 --> 00:06:00,611
No! No, Jean!

59
00:06:00,778 --> 00:06:02,196
No, no, no! Please!

60
00:06:02,321 --> 00:06:03,447
You can't hide.

61
00:06:03,614 --> 00:06:04,615
No, no, no! Please!

62
00:06:04,782 --> 00:06:05,950
You can't hide!

63
00:06:06,116 --> 00:06:07,660
No, Jean! No!

64
00:06:08,369 --> 00:06:09,370
No.

65
00:06:10,621 --> 00:06:12,039
(GASPING)

66
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:14,792
(CLASSICAL MUSIC
PLAYING ON RADIO)

67
00:06:30,808 --> 00:06:32,059
(SIGHS)

68
00:06:37,565 --> 00:06:38,983
(RADIO STATIC)

69
00:07:17,229 --> 00:07:18,647
(GROWLING)

70
00:07:49,428 --> 00:07:51,430
<i>(SIX FEET UNDER</i>
PLAYING ON STEREO)

71
00:08:00,189 --> 00:08:01,690
(MEN TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

72
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:09,573
Whack all of that
on store credit.
Thanks, honey.

73
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:14,495
Got the arrows?
Yeah.

74
00:08:14,578 --> 00:08:15,621
(CAR HORN HONKING)

75
00:08:16,163 --> 00:08:17,289
EDDIE: Remember the arrows?

76
00:08:17,456 --> 00:08:20,250
Yeah, yeah, Eddie,
we got them!

77
00:08:23,962 --> 00:08:25,631
<i>(SIX FEET UNDER</i>
CONTINUES PLAYING)

78
00:08:25,756 --> 00:08:26,715
Yeah!

79
00:08:26,799 --> 00:08:28,050
(MEN WHOOPING)

80
00:08:28,384 --> 00:08:29,343
(GUNSHOT)
(MAN 1 GROANS)

81
00:08:29,426 --> 00:08:30,552
MAN 2: Hey!

82
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:32,638
What are you doing?

83
00:08:32,805 --> 00:08:34,348
Man, you almost
blew his foot off!

84
00:08:34,765 --> 00:08:36,433
You're not a hunter,
are you?

85
00:08:37,601 --> 00:08:39,103
Not anymore.

86
00:08:40,771 --> 00:08:42,147
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

87
00:08:47,778 --> 00:08:49,154
(MAN SCREAMS)

88
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,865
(GUNSHOT)
(MAN SCREAMS)

89
00:09:17,182 --> 00:09:18,767
(DOG BARKING)

90
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:33,532
(BEAR GROWLING)

91
00:09:37,494 --> 00:09:39,496
What the hell?

92
00:09:40,998 --> 00:09:42,416
(ROARS)

93
00:09:52,468 --> 00:09:54,219
(WHIMPERING)

94
00:09:57,347 --> 00:09:58,932
Don't make me do this.

95
00:10:05,564 --> 00:10:07,900
(ROARING)

96
00:10:34,301 --> 00:10:36,553
<i>(LOW</i> PLAYING)

97
00:10:41,058 --> 00:10:43,811
It must have been
damn near 12 feet tall.

98
00:10:43,977 --> 00:10:47,397
We didn't hear
nothing except twigs.

99
00:10:47,815 --> 00:10:49,191
Then it just
came upon us.

100
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:54,363
It got Riley,
just gutted him.
It got Eddie.

101
00:10:55,239 --> 00:10:58,992
Ripped through the tent,
knocked over the snowcat
like it was a toy.

102
00:10:59,868 --> 00:11:01,912
You the one was attacked
by the grizzly?

103
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,750
I'm the one
that survived.

104
00:11:13,882 --> 00:11:16,552
I'd like to buy
this man a drink.

105
00:11:19,263 --> 00:11:20,347
What's your name,
mister?

106
00:11:26,353 --> 00:11:27,437
(GROANS)

107
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,109
It's Logan.

108
00:11:32,943 --> 00:11:37,406
And that's a poison
broadhead, which,
last I heard, was illegal.

109
00:11:38,407 --> 00:11:39,700
(GLASS SHATTERING)

110
00:11:39,783 --> 00:11:41,243
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

111
00:11:45,831 --> 00:11:47,249
(GROANING)

112
00:11:48,792 --> 00:11:51,628
Go ahead,
ask me where I found it.

113
00:11:57,467 --> 00:11:59,136
(GROANING LOUDLY)

114
00:12:00,804 --> 00:12:02,556
Ask me.

115
00:12:03,098 --> 00:12:04,308
Where did you find it?

116
00:12:04,474 --> 00:12:06,476
Well,
funny you should ask.

117
00:12:06,643 --> 00:12:08,812
I pulled it out of
the back of a grizzly.

118
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:12,482
Whoever shot it,
didn't have the wind
or the balls

119
00:12:12,566 --> 00:12:13,984
to track
the animal properly...

120
00:12:14,151 --> 00:12:15,152
and put it out
of its misery.

121
00:12:15,235 --> 00:12:16,445
(GROANS)

122
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:21,491
Instead of dropping
a lethal dose
of the poison...

123
00:12:21,658 --> 00:12:25,579
it bled into the bear,
made him crazy,
killed five people.

124
00:12:25,746 --> 00:12:27,414
I don't know what
you're talking about.

125
00:12:27,581 --> 00:12:29,291
Because I don't dip
my arrows in anything.

126
00:12:30,167 --> 00:12:32,502
In that case,
you got nothing
to worry about.

127
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:37,841
(GRUNTS)

128
00:12:38,592 --> 00:12:39,593
Damn.

129
00:12:46,642 --> 00:12:48,268
That hurt.
(GLASS CLATTERS)

130
00:12:50,187 --> 00:12:51,188
Sorry, Jean.

131
00:12:53,357 --> 00:12:55,651
I wouldn't
bother with them.

132
00:12:55,817 --> 00:12:58,946
Most of them will
die soon anyway,
without your help.

133
00:12:59,529 --> 00:13:02,991
Three of them,
a week from now
in the same truck.

134
00:13:04,368 --> 00:13:05,452
(GRUNTS)

135
00:13:09,539 --> 00:13:10,874
(COUGHING)

136
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:23,637
This sword is
hundreds of years old...

137
00:13:23,804 --> 00:13:27,182
and was named <i>Danzan</i>
by the first samurai
who used it.

138
00:13:27,349 --> 00:13:30,185
<i>Danzan</i> means
"separator"
in Japanese.

139
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:36,400
The ideal weapon
for separating head
and limb from body.

140
00:13:45,784 --> 00:13:47,077
Whoa!

141
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:49,204
Like so.

142
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:51,039
(GLASS CLATTERING)

143
00:13:51,373 --> 00:13:53,583
I'm parked in back.

144
00:14:02,259 --> 00:14:03,719
Get in.
(ENGINE STARTS)

145
00:14:05,429 --> 00:14:07,180
(POLICE SIREN WAILING)

146
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,733
Sorry, it's a rental.

147
00:14:20,277 --> 00:14:21,611
Who are you?

148
00:14:21,778 --> 00:14:24,448
Me? I'm Yukio.

149
00:14:24,614 --> 00:14:26,074
And?

150
00:14:26,616 --> 00:14:28,785
I've been trying
to find you
for over a year.

151
00:14:29,327 --> 00:14:30,495
Why?

152
00:14:30,662 --> 00:14:32,622
To give you that.

153
00:14:33,331 --> 00:14:35,125
My employer
wanted you to have it.

154
00:14:36,793 --> 00:14:38,128
Who's your employer?

155
00:14:38,754 --> 00:14:40,338
Master Yashida.

156
00:14:54,644 --> 00:14:59,441
He said it belongs
to you, and that
he's paying all debts.

157
00:15:00,108 --> 00:15:02,110
Master Yashida is dying.

158
00:15:02,486 --> 00:15:06,114
He wants to say thank you
for saving his life
all those years ago.

159
00:15:06,990 --> 00:15:08,700
He knows that
you are a...

160
00:15:09,826 --> 00:15:10,952
busy man.

161
00:15:11,119 --> 00:15:14,623
But he very much
wants to say his
goodbye in person.

162
00:15:14,998 --> 00:15:16,666
All right,
where is he?

163
00:15:16,833 --> 00:15:18,126
Tokyo.

164
00:15:18,293 --> 00:15:20,378
Wait...
I'm not going to Japan.

165
00:15:20,545 --> 00:15:23,048
It would be
dishonorable for you
to refuse his request.

166
00:15:23,215 --> 00:15:27,302
Well, apologize
to Mr. Yashida,
I'm not going to Tokyo.

167
00:15:27,469 --> 00:15:29,012
All right?
I've got things to do.

168
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:30,514
Do not apologize.

169
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,183
It's been an honor
just to meet
the Wolverine.

170
00:15:36,311 --> 00:15:38,730
That's not
who I am anymore,
you understand?

171
00:15:40,649 --> 00:15:41,733
Interesting.

172
00:15:43,193 --> 00:15:45,695
Why did you go
into that bar,
if not to seek justice?

173
00:15:45,862 --> 00:15:46,863
I don't know.
You don't know.

174
00:15:46,988 --> 00:15:48,240
No!
I think you know.

175
00:15:48,406 --> 00:15:50,408
Pull over.
You are a soldier.

176
00:15:50,575 --> 00:15:51,827
No, I'm not.
Pull over.

177
00:15:51,993 --> 00:15:53,036
You are a soldier.

178
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:54,830
Pull over, now!

179
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,331
Now.

180
00:15:57,374 --> 00:15:58,542
(BRAKES SCREECH)

181
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:04,756
You are a soldier,
and you seek what
all soldiers do.

182
00:16:05,048 --> 00:16:06,049
And what's that?

183
00:16:06,758 --> 00:16:08,718
An honorable death.

184
00:16:08,885 --> 00:16:10,137
An end to your pain.

185
00:16:11,638 --> 00:16:13,390
Who says I'm in pain?

186
00:16:14,641 --> 00:16:18,728
A man who has nightmares
every night of his life
is in pain.

187
00:16:36,454 --> 00:16:37,664
One day.

188
00:16:38,498 --> 00:16:41,835
I say goodbye
to Mr. Yashida and
I come right back.

189
00:16:43,003 --> 00:16:44,588
Okay.

190
00:16:50,468 --> 00:16:53,597
Fifteen hours.
Depending on the wind.

191
00:16:54,347 --> 00:16:55,849
Fifteen hours?

192
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:58,351
You don't like to fly?

193
00:16:58,935 --> 00:17:00,437
I love it.

194
00:17:07,944 --> 00:17:09,446
(EXHALES)

195
00:17:18,622 --> 00:17:19,956
(SIGHS)

196
00:17:27,088 --> 00:17:28,298
YOUNG YASHIDA:
<i>Kuzuri.</i>

197
00:17:29,341 --> 00:17:30,550
<i>Kuzuri.</i>

198
00:17:31,468 --> 00:17:32,469
<i>Kuzuri.</i>

199
00:17:36,556 --> 00:17:38,475
<i>Kuzuri.</i>
What does that mean?

200
00:17:38,558 --> 00:17:39,935
Monster.

201
00:17:42,145 --> 00:17:44,356
No pain?

202
00:17:45,273 --> 00:17:48,068
You have no...
Oh, yeah. Pain.

203
00:17:48,944 --> 00:17:50,487
Plenty of pain.

204
00:17:54,824 --> 00:17:56,576
How old are you?

205
00:17:57,535 --> 00:17:59,371
It's been
a long time.

206
00:18:00,747 --> 00:18:02,082
Many wars.

207
00:18:02,958 --> 00:18:04,292
Understand?

208
00:18:07,003 --> 00:18:08,171
(SIGHS)

209
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,757
Too many
fuckin' wars.

210
00:18:18,265 --> 00:18:19,683
(EXHALES)

211
00:18:21,434 --> 00:18:22,978
We are almost there.

212
00:18:24,354 --> 00:18:25,897
So, you can
see the future?

213
00:18:26,982 --> 00:18:28,942
I can read a map.

214
00:18:29,651 --> 00:18:32,696
You said you knew
the future of those
assholes in the bar.

215
00:18:33,363 --> 00:18:35,532
I know
they are going to die.

216
00:18:36,449 --> 00:18:38,535
We are all going to die.

217
00:18:38,827 --> 00:18:42,205
You said they would
die in the same truck,
in a week.

218
00:18:42,789 --> 00:18:44,874
If you're right,
that's quite a talent.

219
00:18:48,336 --> 00:18:50,213
We don't all have claws.

220
00:18:52,215 --> 00:18:53,550
(SIGHS)

221
00:18:53,633 --> 00:18:56,219
So, do I die
on this plane?

222
00:18:57,721 --> 00:18:58,888
No.

223
00:19:00,056 --> 00:19:01,349
Not on this plane.

224
00:19:25,832 --> 00:19:27,125
(FEMALE ANNOUNCER
SPEAKING JAPANESE ON SPEAKER)

225
00:19:27,208 --> 00:19:28,918
YUKIO: Don't let
the lights fool you.

226
00:19:29,377 --> 00:19:31,129
These are dark days
in Japan.

227
00:19:31,921 --> 00:19:34,507
Some believe
when Master Yashida
got sick,

228
00:19:34,591 --> 00:19:35,759
a shadow fell upon us.

229
00:19:36,259 --> 00:19:37,927
Do you think
he's a god?

230
00:19:39,554 --> 00:19:41,389
No. A man.

231
00:19:41,806 --> 00:19:43,141
But a great one.

232
00:19:43,558 --> 00:19:46,436
After the war,
he helped rebuild
the nation.

233
00:19:46,770 --> 00:19:49,189
And the family business
became Japan's largest.

234
00:19:49,397 --> 00:19:52,484
Wow. Did they
give you a little
card to memorize?

235
00:19:54,444 --> 00:19:56,446
I owe Master Yashida
my life.

236
00:19:56,988 --> 00:19:58,531
Don't be a dick.

237
00:20:09,334 --> 00:20:11,294
(RADIO CHATTER)

238
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:15,090
A lot of guns.

239
00:20:15,173 --> 00:20:16,674
There have been attacks.

240
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:19,552
Attempted kidnappings.
Attempted assassinations.

241
00:20:19,719 --> 00:20:21,054
By who?

242
00:20:21,179 --> 00:20:23,723
The Japanese mob,
the Yakuza.

243
00:20:23,932 --> 00:20:26,601
They've grown strong
as the government
has grown weak.

244
00:20:26,684 --> 00:20:28,311
(ALARM BEEPING)
(ALL SPEAKING JAPANESE)

245
00:20:30,313 --> 00:20:31,856
Hip replacement.

246
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:41,282
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

247
00:20:41,366 --> 00:20:42,742
Uh, too small.

248
00:20:44,369 --> 00:20:45,787
Too small.

249
00:21:02,470 --> 00:21:04,055
(MEN GRUNTING)

250
00:21:12,522 --> 00:21:13,690
Hey.

251
00:21:15,024 --> 00:21:16,067
This way.

252
00:21:17,068 --> 00:21:18,528
Who's that?

253
00:21:22,198 --> 00:21:24,576
Shingen,
Master Yashida's son.

254
00:21:28,204 --> 00:21:29,205
He's good.

255
00:21:31,541 --> 00:21:32,709
He's all right.

256
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:37,338
(BOTH GREETING IN JAPANESE)

257
00:21:37,672 --> 00:21:40,383
So, what happened
to the badass in boots?

258
00:21:40,550 --> 00:21:42,719
Master Yashida
is traditional.

259
00:21:42,886 --> 00:21:45,889
One eye on the past
and the other on the future.

260
00:21:46,806 --> 00:21:47,891
(DOOR LOCK BEEPS)

261
00:21:48,683 --> 00:21:50,477
(YASHIDA SPEAKING
SOFTLY IN JAPANESE)

262
00:21:56,024 --> 00:21:57,275
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

263
00:22:00,570 --> 00:22:03,907
That's Mariko,
his granddaughter.

264
00:22:07,744 --> 00:22:08,995
(GLASS CLATTERING)

265
00:22:23,051 --> 00:22:24,260
Mariko.

266
00:22:24,677 --> 00:22:25,720
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

267
00:22:25,803 --> 00:22:27,388
What's wrong with you?

268
00:22:29,599 --> 00:22:31,100
(SOBBING)

269
00:22:36,606 --> 00:22:39,067
You haven't answered my emails.

270
00:22:39,776 --> 00:22:41,319
I can't tell you now.

271
00:22:42,403 --> 00:22:44,030
Yes, you can.

272
00:22:48,576 --> 00:22:50,495
Who is the caveman?

273
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,790
The man Grandfather wanted me to find.

274
00:22:54,916 --> 00:22:57,126
You can't bring him in like that.

275
00:23:06,803 --> 00:23:09,806
Shizu and Saki
are going to
disinfect you.

276
00:23:11,683 --> 00:23:12,684
Give you a shave.

277
00:23:12,809 --> 00:23:14,352
Like hell they are.

278
00:23:14,852 --> 00:23:16,354
Get in the tub.
(SIGHS)

279
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:17,981
Whoa.

280
00:23:18,147 --> 00:23:20,275
Get in the tub.

281
00:23:21,150 --> 00:23:22,318
Really?

282
00:23:23,653 --> 00:23:25,947
(WOMEN SHOUTING
IN JAPANESE)

283
00:23:26,030 --> 00:23:27,323
All right.

284
00:23:31,327 --> 00:23:33,788
Okay. Okay.

285
00:23:33,955 --> 00:23:36,332
All right,
all right, all right.
I can do that bit.

286
00:23:37,625 --> 00:23:39,085
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

287
00:23:47,218 --> 00:23:48,469
What?

288
00:23:50,513 --> 00:23:51,723
What?

289
00:23:52,473 --> 00:23:53,891
You look nice.

290
00:23:54,559 --> 00:23:56,519
I feel violated.

291
00:23:57,520 --> 00:24:00,356
DR. GREEN: Prepare
two more suppressors
for Master Yashida.

292
00:24:00,690 --> 00:24:02,400
And check
his blood pressure.

293
00:24:19,042 --> 00:24:20,668
Yashida-<i>sama.</i>

294
00:24:20,793 --> 00:24:22,337
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

295
00:24:26,674 --> 00:24:27,759
Oh...

296
00:24:29,218 --> 00:24:30,219
<i>Kuzuri.</i>

297
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:32,680
You look the same.

298
00:24:33,514 --> 00:24:35,183
But, then,
that is no surprise.

299
00:24:38,394 --> 00:24:39,979
Dr. Green.

300
00:24:40,647 --> 00:24:42,649
Leave us, please.

301
00:24:43,399 --> 00:24:45,193
Five minutes,
no more.

302
00:24:48,738 --> 00:24:50,156
My oncologist.

303
00:24:50,907 --> 00:24:51,991
Well done.

304
00:24:55,745 --> 00:24:59,749
Oh, forget the etiquette.
I'm past such precautions.

305
00:25:01,417 --> 00:25:02,669
(EXHALES)

306
00:25:05,630 --> 00:25:10,343
For many years
I have wanted to thank you
for saving my life.

307
00:25:11,678 --> 00:25:12,845
Yeah, well...

308
00:25:14,222 --> 00:25:15,723
You were kind to me.

309
00:25:16,724 --> 00:25:18,601
And you were kind
to many people.

310
00:25:19,268 --> 00:25:21,145
I saw that even
from that well.

311
00:25:24,148 --> 00:25:25,233
(GROANS SOFTLY)

312
00:25:28,903 --> 00:25:30,113
(EXHALES)

313
00:25:40,957 --> 00:25:44,335
YASHIDA: The painting
is from the village
of my birth.

314
00:25:44,919 --> 00:25:49,132
It depicts
the bravery and skill
of the Black Clan.

315
00:25:49,298 --> 00:25:51,759
Ninja warriors.

316
00:25:51,926 --> 00:25:54,971
They served my family
for seven centuries.

317
00:25:56,681 --> 00:26:00,309
I didn't send for you
only to thank you, Logan.

318
00:26:02,103 --> 00:26:03,980
I wanted to repay you.

319
00:26:06,774 --> 00:26:09,652
To offer you something
no one else can.

320
00:26:10,611 --> 00:26:13,948
A gift to equal
the life you gave to me.

321
00:26:14,365 --> 00:26:15,825
I don't need anything.

322
00:26:15,992 --> 00:26:17,452
Not a thing.

323
00:26:18,161 --> 00:26:20,830
Eternity can be a curse.

324
00:26:21,956 --> 00:26:24,709
It hasn't been
easy for you,
living without time.

325
00:26:25,668 --> 00:26:27,670
The losses you
have had to suffer.

326
00:26:28,171 --> 00:26:31,048
A man can run out
of things to live for.

327
00:26:31,841 --> 00:26:33,468
Lose his purpose.

328
00:26:33,634 --> 00:26:35,344
Become a ronin.

329
00:26:36,804 --> 00:26:39,849
A samurai without a master.

330
00:26:44,562 --> 00:26:47,023
I can end your eternity.

331
00:26:47,857 --> 00:26:49,066
Make you mortal.

332
00:26:51,861 --> 00:26:57,033
What they did to me,
what I am, can't be undone.

333
00:26:57,200 --> 00:27:00,203
Yashida Industries
can do anything.

334
00:27:00,828 --> 00:27:05,374
We have reason
to believe your ability
to heal can be passed.

335
00:27:05,541 --> 00:27:06,542
Passed?

336
00:27:06,709 --> 00:27:08,211
From you to another.

337
00:27:10,671 --> 00:27:11,631
(SIGHS)

338
00:27:11,714 --> 00:27:14,842
You have struggled
long enough, Logan.

339
00:27:16,344 --> 00:27:17,428
I'm confused.

340
00:27:17,595 --> 00:27:21,224
I came here to say goodbye
to a man I once knew.

341
00:27:21,390 --> 00:27:23,100
I am the same man.

342
00:27:23,267 --> 00:27:25,770
I was not ready
to die then.

343
00:27:25,937 --> 00:27:28,439
I am not ready
to die now.

344
00:27:29,232 --> 00:27:30,441
But you are...

345
00:27:31,692 --> 00:27:33,444
aren't you?

346
00:27:35,530 --> 00:27:37,740
Are you offering to kill me?
No.

347
00:27:37,907 --> 00:27:39,742
Not right away.

348
00:27:40,451 --> 00:27:43,579
You can live a long
and ordinary life.

349
00:27:44,205 --> 00:27:46,791
Fall in love,
have a family...

350
00:27:46,958 --> 00:27:48,876
grow old.

351
00:27:49,919 --> 00:27:54,173
And one day,
die an ordinary death.

352
00:27:58,594 --> 00:28:00,054
It can be done.

353
00:28:01,430 --> 00:28:05,601
Yeah, look,
nice to see you again.
Sorry you got sick.

354
00:28:05,768 --> 00:28:08,813
Please, Logan-<i>san.</i>
I need you again.

355
00:28:08,980 --> 00:28:11,440
I fear for my family.
(HEART MONITOR
BEEPING RAPIDLY)

356
00:28:11,607 --> 00:28:14,068
I fear for everything
I have built.

357
00:28:14,235 --> 00:28:16,404
Enough.
You should leave.
Please, Logan-<i>san.</i>

358
00:28:16,571 --> 00:28:17,989
They're going
to kill her.

359
00:28:18,155 --> 00:28:18,823
Who?

360
00:28:19,156 --> 00:28:21,284
Mariko, my granddaughter.

361
00:28:21,659 --> 00:28:25,288
She is my treasure.
She must be protected.

362
00:28:28,624 --> 00:28:31,252
You don't want
what I've got.

363
00:28:31,335 --> 00:28:32,753
(MONITOR CONTINUES
BEEPING RAPIDLY)

364
00:28:33,087 --> 00:28:34,255
<i>Kuzuri.</i>

365
00:28:34,630 --> 00:28:35,840
<i>Kuzuri!</i>

366
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:38,801
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

367
00:28:38,885 --> 00:28:42,930
Lord Shingen, your father is asking for you.

368
00:28:45,016 --> 00:28:46,934
It is time.

369
00:28:52,273 --> 00:28:54,317
(MARIKO SPEAKING JAPANESE)

370
00:28:56,527 --> 00:28:59,655
I need to speak with my father...

371
00:29:00,031 --> 00:29:03,159
before he speaks to Grandfather.

372
00:29:03,492 --> 00:29:05,328
He'll talk to you later, Mariko.

373
00:29:05,453 --> 00:29:06,996
Father! I need to see you now!

374
00:29:07,204 --> 00:29:08,956
Not now, Mariko!

375
00:29:14,837 --> 00:29:16,380
(SHINGEN AND MARIKO
ARGUING IN JAPANESE)

376
00:29:50,539 --> 00:29:52,041
(MEN SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

377
00:29:56,671 --> 00:29:57,880
(GASPING)

378
00:29:58,839 --> 00:30:01,008
Careful, careful.
It's slippery out here.

379
00:30:02,218 --> 00:30:03,344
Let go.

380
00:30:04,178 --> 00:30:05,179
(PANTING)

381
00:30:05,721 --> 00:30:07,264
You about done?

382
00:30:08,557 --> 00:30:10,726
Let go of me.

383
00:30:19,902 --> 00:30:21,654
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

384
00:30:30,579 --> 00:30:33,290
He just wanted
to say goodbye, huh?

385
00:30:41,090 --> 00:30:42,383
You two
grew up together.

386
00:30:43,050 --> 00:30:44,218
Yes.

387
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:46,554
But you're not
her sister.

388
00:30:47,930 --> 00:30:49,056
No.

389
00:30:51,934 --> 00:30:54,562
Master Yashida found me
on a trip to the South.

390
00:30:55,438 --> 00:30:58,441
He brought Mariko
to see a factory
he was building.

391
00:31:01,652 --> 00:31:04,989
I was digging
through the garbage
for something to eat.

392
00:31:06,949 --> 00:31:08,617
So they just took
you home with them?

393
00:31:09,994 --> 00:31:13,330
It was always
difficult for Mariko
to make friends.

394
00:31:22,798 --> 00:31:25,134
I'll see to it the plane
is ready in the morning.

395
00:31:25,676 --> 00:31:27,511
Sleep here.

396
00:31:45,237 --> 00:31:46,238
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

397
00:31:46,322 --> 00:31:49,241
Don't look so sad, Shingen.

398
00:31:50,284 --> 00:31:52,161
I'm still dying.

399
00:31:52,620 --> 00:31:55,206
I'll be in my office
if you need me.

400
00:32:00,628 --> 00:32:01,629
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

401
00:32:01,712 --> 00:32:05,174
There is no easy way to say this.

402
00:32:06,717 --> 00:32:10,971
But then, it's never been easy for us, has it?

403
00:32:12,223 --> 00:32:14,266
I have tried, father.

404
00:32:14,600 --> 00:32:16,852
You've done the best you can.

405
00:32:26,195 --> 00:32:29,865
You have always been
my assumed successor.

406
00:32:30,866 --> 00:32:33,202
So the past few years,
as a test,

407
00:32:33,285 --> 00:32:35,246
I allowed you
more control.

408
00:32:36,372 --> 00:32:37,790
It has been an honor.

409
00:32:37,873 --> 00:32:41,085
And I now realize
that was a mistake.

410
00:32:42,253 --> 00:32:45,756
You have brought
this company
close to ruin.

411
00:32:46,632 --> 00:32:48,467
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

412
00:32:48,551 --> 00:32:52,721
When I die,
someone else will take
my place as chairman.

413
00:32:56,100 --> 00:33:00,146
Father,
I'm sorry if I have
disappointed you...

414
00:33:00,229 --> 00:33:02,231
Let's not insult
one another.

415
00:33:03,440 --> 00:33:06,694
You are not the man
to lead Yashida.

416
00:33:09,655 --> 00:33:12,491
You cannot bring in
someone from the outside.

417
00:33:13,617 --> 00:33:15,786
In that,
you are correct.

418
00:33:17,997 --> 00:33:19,331
(SNICKERS)

419
00:33:27,673 --> 00:33:29,550
(LAUGHS INCREDULOUSLY)

420
00:33:36,223 --> 00:33:37,224
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

421
00:33:37,308 --> 00:33:40,019
That will never happen.

422
00:33:40,102 --> 00:33:41,854
(HEART MONITOR
BEEPING RAPIDLY)

423
00:33:47,443 --> 00:33:48,944
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

424
00:33:52,907 --> 00:33:55,868
YASHIDA: <i>Eternity
can be a curse...</i>

425
00:33:56,785 --> 00:33:58,037
<i>Kuzuri.</i>

426
00:33:58,204 --> 00:34:01,582
YOUNG YASHIDA:
<i>You have no pain, Kuzuri?</i>

427
00:34:01,790 --> 00:34:02,791
How old are you?

428
00:34:03,459 --> 00:34:04,919
JEAN GREY: Interesting offer.

429
00:34:08,797 --> 00:34:11,425
What are you doing
turning the old man down?

430
00:34:12,134 --> 00:34:14,637
I thought you
wanted to be with me.

431
00:34:15,137 --> 00:34:16,096
Come here.

432
00:34:33,822 --> 00:34:34,990
(GRUNTS)

433
00:34:35,950 --> 00:34:37,326
(GAGGING)

434
00:34:38,410 --> 00:34:39,787
(GASPING)

435
00:34:43,374 --> 00:34:44,708
(SHOUTS)

436
00:34:45,751 --> 00:34:47,253
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

437
00:34:47,419 --> 00:34:48,963
(WOMAN SOBBING)
(FOOTSTEPS RETREATING)

438
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:53,384
(WOMAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

439
00:34:56,637 --> 00:34:58,097
(MEN SPEAKING JAPANESE)

440
00:35:06,897 --> 00:35:07,898
YUKIO: He's dead.

441
00:35:11,151 --> 00:35:13,279
I didn't foresee it.

442
00:35:14,989 --> 00:35:16,448
(CAMERAS CLICKING)

443
00:35:30,713 --> 00:35:32,464
(BOTH SPEAKING JAPANESE)

444
00:35:41,682 --> 00:35:43,017
(GUARDS CHATTERING
INDISTINCTLY)

445
00:36:31,023 --> 00:36:32,566
(ALL CHANTING)

446
00:36:49,249 --> 00:36:51,752
Who's that?
With Mariko.

447
00:36:51,919 --> 00:36:53,420
His name is Noburo Mori.

448
00:36:53,587 --> 00:36:56,131
Minister of Justice,
a rising star.

449
00:36:56,298 --> 00:36:58,884
He's Mariko's fiancé.

450
00:36:59,051 --> 00:37:01,053
You need to bow.

451
00:37:07,434 --> 00:37:08,519
(WHISPERS)
Bow.

452
00:37:08,602 --> 00:37:09,728
(CLEARS THROAT)

453
00:37:13,190 --> 00:37:15,067
YUKIO: Lord Shingen,
this is Mr. Logan.

454
00:37:15,234 --> 00:37:17,111
I know who he is.

455
00:37:17,653 --> 00:37:19,405
Your father
was a good man.

456
00:37:19,488 --> 00:37:20,531
(SCOFFS)

457
00:37:20,823 --> 00:37:23,200
He would often say
the same about you.

458
00:37:24,576 --> 00:37:28,080
But then, he was always
fascinated with your kind.

459
00:37:29,873 --> 00:37:34,336
Tell me, why do you
think he sent our
little Yukio to fetch you?

460
00:37:36,338 --> 00:37:37,798
To say goodbye.

461
00:37:39,466 --> 00:37:41,635
And now you have.

462
00:37:42,344 --> 00:37:44,847
Time for you to go
back to your cave.

463
00:37:51,186 --> 00:37:53,021
(GONG BANGING)

464
00:38:00,612 --> 00:38:02,990
Anyone else
you want me to meet?

465
00:38:21,300 --> 00:38:22,342
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

466
00:38:22,426 --> 00:38:24,303
I pledge to you...

467
00:38:24,887 --> 00:38:26,388
Master Yashida...

468
00:38:27,681 --> 00:38:29,558
to be vigilant...

469
00:38:29,892 --> 00:38:31,685
and to dedicate my life...

470
00:38:31,894 --> 00:38:33,854
to protect Mariko.

471
00:38:39,818 --> 00:38:42,070
YUKIO: That armor belonged
to <i>Shiruba-Samurai...</i>

472
00:38:42,237 --> 00:38:44,573
the Silver Samurai.

473
00:38:44,740 --> 00:38:48,118
It will stand watch
over the old man forever.

474
00:39:04,968 --> 00:39:06,470
Logan?

475
00:39:12,184 --> 00:39:14,102
Hey.
Something's not right.

476
00:39:15,854 --> 00:39:17,314
Let go.

477
00:39:17,439 --> 00:39:18,774
(GUARD SPEAKING JAPANESE)

478
00:39:21,944 --> 00:39:23,403
(SHOUTS IN JAPANESE)

479
00:39:31,954 --> 00:39:33,372
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

480
00:39:33,455 --> 00:39:34,623
(YELLS)

481
00:39:34,706 --> 00:39:36,124
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

482
00:39:39,795 --> 00:39:41,296
(EXHALES)

483
00:39:41,797 --> 00:39:42,839
(YELLS)

484
00:39:44,466 --> 00:39:45,509
Logan!
(GUNFIRE)

485
00:39:48,053 --> 00:39:49,805
Logan!
(GROANING)

486
00:39:51,265 --> 00:39:52,391
(YELLING)

487
00:39:55,477 --> 00:39:56,562
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

488
00:39:59,439 --> 00:40:00,691
(GRUNTS)

489
00:40:02,192 --> 00:40:03,735
(PEOPLE CONTINUE SCREAMING)

490
00:40:08,115 --> 00:40:09,491
(GUNFIRE)

491
00:40:11,159 --> 00:40:12,286
(GRUNTS)

492
00:40:16,331 --> 00:40:17,332
Logan!

493
00:40:36,518 --> 00:40:37,978
(GASPING)

494
00:40:39,938 --> 00:40:41,690
(MAN SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

495
00:40:49,448 --> 00:40:50,741
(SCREAMS)

496
00:40:54,161 --> 00:40:55,537
(GROANS)

497
00:40:58,749 --> 00:41:00,000
(GRUNTS)

498
00:41:04,504 --> 00:41:05,547
(SCREAMS)

499
00:41:07,299 --> 00:41:08,717
(GUNFIRE)

500
00:41:14,348 --> 00:41:15,557
(PANTING)

501
00:41:15,891 --> 00:41:17,726
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)
(GRUNTING)

502
00:41:34,159 --> 00:41:35,869
(MEN SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

503
00:41:56,139 --> 00:41:57,140
(GROANS)

504
00:41:57,849 --> 00:41:59,017
<i>Kuzuri.</i>

505
00:42:01,103 --> 00:42:02,604
Let's go.
Come on, let's go!

506
00:42:16,076 --> 00:42:17,494
Yukio!
Mariko!

507
00:42:17,577 --> 00:42:18,704
(SPEAKS JAPANESE)

508
00:42:21,790 --> 00:42:23,125
(GUNSHOTS)

509
00:42:45,897 --> 00:42:47,441
(METAL CLANGING)

510
00:43:02,247 --> 00:43:03,790
(GROANS)

511
00:43:07,502 --> 00:43:09,045
Mariko!

512
00:43:10,046 --> 00:43:11,673
(MEN SHOUTING)

513
00:43:26,730 --> 00:43:28,106
(CAR HORN BLARING)

514
00:43:28,899 --> 00:43:30,317
(WOMAN SCREAMS)

515
00:43:36,490 --> 00:43:38,366
(MEN SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

516
00:44:00,722 --> 00:44:02,265
Come on.
Let's go, let's go.

517
00:44:02,766 --> 00:44:04,267
(GUNSHOTS)
(WOMAN SCREAMS)

518
00:44:12,234 --> 00:44:13,360
(GROANS)

519
00:44:28,500 --> 00:44:29,668
(GROANS)

520
00:44:32,170 --> 00:44:33,171
(YELLING)

521
00:44:33,255 --> 00:44:34,840
(GUNFIRE CONTINUES)

522
00:44:42,222 --> 00:44:43,849
Here, here! Here!

523
00:44:44,349 --> 00:44:46,142
(LIVELY SLOT MACHINE
MUSIC PLAYING)

524
00:44:48,937 --> 00:44:50,021
(GROANS)

525
00:44:58,071 --> 00:44:59,239
Move!

526
00:45:00,073 --> 00:45:02,200
In here! Move!
(GUNFIRE)

527
00:45:02,909 --> 00:45:04,244
(MAN SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

528
00:45:04,786 --> 00:45:05,787
(BANGS)
(GRUNTS)

529
00:45:05,871 --> 00:45:07,330
(BOTH PANTING)

530
00:45:12,460 --> 00:45:14,045
(CHOKING)

531
00:45:18,133 --> 00:45:19,467
Keep moving,
keep moving.

532
00:45:20,135 --> 00:45:21,761
Move!

533
00:45:22,470 --> 00:45:24,139
(PEOPLE CLAMORING)

534
00:45:26,224 --> 00:45:27,517
(POLICE SIREN WAILING)

535
00:45:30,812 --> 00:45:32,439
You're bleeding.
You need help.

536
00:45:32,606 --> 00:45:34,107
Just keep moving.

537
00:45:36,318 --> 00:45:37,736
(PANTING)

538
00:45:38,111 --> 00:45:39,696
(WOMAN CHATTERING ON PA)

539
00:45:43,283 --> 00:45:45,160
Thank you for
what you did back there.

540
00:45:45,327 --> 00:45:46,870
Those were Yakuza.
I'm fine.

541
00:45:47,037 --> 00:45:48,705
Why are they after you?

542
00:45:48,872 --> 00:45:51,416
I'm fine. I can make
my way from here.

543
00:45:51,583 --> 00:45:55,211
You should go.
Get yourself a doctor.

544
00:46:03,720 --> 00:46:05,347
(MEN SPEAKING JAPANESE)

545
00:46:38,588 --> 00:46:39,589
(BELL CHIMES)

546
00:46:39,673 --> 00:46:41,216
(MAN CHATTERING ON PA)

547
00:46:44,594 --> 00:46:45,804
(CLATTERS)
Whoa!

548
00:46:45,887 --> 00:46:46,930
(CHUCKLES)

549
00:46:47,013 --> 00:46:48,014
That's nice.

550
00:46:50,517 --> 00:46:52,560
This is one of those
bullet trains, right?

551
00:46:52,727 --> 00:46:54,562
I told you I don't
need your help.

552
00:46:55,897 --> 00:46:58,942
So what do they do,
like, 300 miles an hour?

553
00:47:01,194 --> 00:47:02,904
(AMBULANCE SIREN WAILING)

554
00:47:02,988 --> 00:47:04,823
(CAMERAS CLICKING)
(REPORTERS CLAMORING)

555
00:47:06,908 --> 00:47:08,034
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

556
00:47:08,118 --> 00:47:09,911
This cowardly attack was...

557
00:47:10,245 --> 00:47:12,080
the work of Yakuza thugs.

558
00:47:12,372 --> 00:47:16,376
A violent response to my efforts...

559
00:47:16,501 --> 00:47:19,754
to crack down on organized crime.

560
00:47:22,007 --> 00:47:24,718
They exited the North Gate.

561
00:47:24,968 --> 00:47:27,762
She was with the stranger...

562
00:47:34,602 --> 00:47:36,896
Your <i>gaijin</i> friend,
where is he?

563
00:47:37,397 --> 00:47:39,566
Last I saw,
he was protecting
your daughter.

564
00:47:40,150 --> 00:47:41,443
(SCOFFS)

565
00:47:41,901 --> 00:47:43,653
You are a toy doll.

566
00:47:43,820 --> 00:47:46,948
A companion for a child
who has outgrown you.

567
00:47:47,115 --> 00:47:49,325
Keep that in mind.

568
00:47:49,784 --> 00:47:51,536
(SPEAKS JAPANESE)

569
00:48:01,421 --> 00:48:03,840
So, where are we
headed, Mariko?

570
00:48:08,428 --> 00:48:09,512
Where are we going?

571
00:48:11,139 --> 00:48:13,475
I'm going to the end
of the line.

572
00:48:13,558 --> 00:48:15,894
My family has a home
in the South.

573
00:48:16,436 --> 00:48:17,687
That's stupid.

574
00:48:18,438 --> 00:48:21,316
No offense,
but they're gonna know
to look for you there.

575
00:48:21,649 --> 00:48:23,443
Not this place.

576
00:48:24,444 --> 00:48:25,779
You want
to be left alone.
Yes.

577
00:48:25,945 --> 00:48:27,030
I understand.
Do you?

578
00:48:27,113 --> 00:48:28,615
Oh, yeah.
Trust me.

579
00:48:28,782 --> 00:48:29,866
Problem is,
if I do that...

580
00:48:30,033 --> 00:48:32,118
I don't think you're
gonna live to see
the end of the day.

581
00:48:35,705 --> 00:48:39,501
You can't pretend
shit isn't happening
when it is, princess.

582
00:48:39,667 --> 00:48:43,379
Unless you want to die.
In that case, you're
playing this perfectly.

583
00:48:49,344 --> 00:48:50,512
(GROANS)

584
00:48:51,554 --> 00:48:52,764
(SIGHS)

585
00:49:07,529 --> 00:49:09,197
Oh... What the hell?

586
00:49:10,698 --> 00:49:11,866
(GROANS)

587
00:49:15,120 --> 00:49:16,621
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

588
00:49:18,289 --> 00:49:19,415
Oh...

589
00:49:30,093 --> 00:49:31,678
What the hell is happening?

590
00:49:36,516 --> 00:49:38,143
(MEN SPEAKING JAPANESE)

591
00:49:50,947 --> 00:49:52,031
(YELLS)

592
00:49:52,740 --> 00:49:54,242
(ALL GRUNTING)

593
00:50:01,916 --> 00:50:03,168
(WIND HOWLING)

594
00:50:13,553 --> 00:50:14,762
(SCREAMING)

595
00:50:19,309 --> 00:50:20,602
(YELLS)

596
00:50:26,274 --> 00:50:28,234
(YELLING)

597
00:50:32,405 --> 00:50:33,740
(SCREAMS)

598
00:50:40,246 --> 00:50:41,289
(GASPS)

599
00:51:53,486 --> 00:51:55,530
(MUSIC PLAYING
ON HEADPHONES)

600
00:52:03,204 --> 00:52:04,372
(YELLING)

601
00:52:08,793 --> 00:52:10,211
(SCREAMING)

602
00:52:12,463 --> 00:52:13,881
(YELLING)

603
00:52:17,552 --> 00:52:18,970
(WOMAN CHATTERING ON PA)

604
00:52:19,053 --> 00:52:20,054
(PANTING)

605
00:52:20,138 --> 00:52:21,139
What happened to you?

606
00:52:21,306 --> 00:52:22,890
We get off here.
Let's go.

607
00:52:23,558 --> 00:52:25,810
Just listen to me,
will you? We need
to find someplace safe.

608
00:52:25,977 --> 00:52:28,730
I don't understand.
How do you know
they were Yakuza?

609
00:52:28,896 --> 00:52:30,398
They were the same
guys from the temple.

610
00:52:30,815 --> 00:52:31,899
How do you know
they were after me?

611
00:52:32,066 --> 00:52:33,151
Look, we need to
find someplace safe.

612
00:52:33,234 --> 00:52:34,235
We need to get
off the streets.

613
00:52:34,402 --> 00:52:36,321
I don't understand.
Shut up! Listen.

614
00:52:36,487 --> 00:52:38,906
Do you know this place?
Where's downtown?

615
00:52:39,073 --> 00:52:40,616
Straight ahead.

616
00:52:50,126 --> 00:52:52,128
So, where's
the nice part of town?

617
00:52:52,295 --> 00:52:53,588
Another eight blocks
that way.

618
00:52:53,755 --> 00:52:55,798
Good.
We're staying here.

619
00:52:56,174 --> 00:52:57,759
Let's go.

620
00:53:02,680 --> 00:53:04,766
This is a love hotel.

621
00:53:04,932 --> 00:53:06,309
A what?

622
00:53:06,476 --> 00:53:08,019
A love hotel.

623
00:53:09,270 --> 00:53:11,939
For couples,
understand?

624
00:53:12,774 --> 00:53:14,484
Uh... Right.

625
00:53:15,276 --> 00:53:16,444
Hey.

626
00:53:16,611 --> 00:53:20,782
Uh, two rooms.
Adjoining rooms,
on the same floor.

627
00:53:21,032 --> 00:53:23,326
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)
Right next to each other.
Very close.

628
00:53:23,951 --> 00:53:25,870
Same floor. Same floor.

629
00:53:28,122 --> 00:53:29,207
(SIGHS)

630
00:53:29,290 --> 00:53:30,666
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

631
00:53:44,972 --> 00:53:46,140
What did she say?

632
00:53:47,016 --> 00:53:50,144
She has no rooms
available next
to each other.

633
00:53:50,311 --> 00:53:55,233
She's asking if we prefer
"the dungeon",
"the nurse's office..."

634
00:53:56,025 --> 00:53:58,694
Or the "mission to Mars."

635
00:54:04,951 --> 00:54:06,828
(WOMAN GIGGLING)
(BED CREAKING)

636
00:54:14,752 --> 00:54:16,212
This'll do.

637
00:54:20,258 --> 00:54:22,427
MAN ON SPEAKERS:
<i>Liftoff! We have a liftoff!</i>

638
00:54:22,593 --> 00:54:24,762
Kind of homey,
actually.

639
00:54:32,103 --> 00:54:33,771
Where do you plan
on sleeping?

640
00:54:36,399 --> 00:54:37,316
I don't.

641
00:54:40,278 --> 00:54:41,863
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

642
00:54:48,828 --> 00:54:49,829
(SHATTERS)

643
00:55:12,727 --> 00:55:14,228
JEAN GREY:
That's a lot of blood.

644
00:55:16,898 --> 00:55:19,817
I thought you were
done being the hero.

645
00:55:20,443 --> 00:55:23,446
But these guys were...
trying to kill her.

646
00:55:26,199 --> 00:55:28,242
Just let it go.

647
00:55:29,702 --> 00:55:31,370
It's not hard to die.

648
00:55:34,165 --> 00:55:36,000
Come to me.

649
00:55:45,843 --> 00:55:47,595
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

650
00:55:48,095 --> 00:55:50,014
(MEN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

651
00:55:52,141 --> 00:55:53,142
Eh!

652
00:55:53,601 --> 00:55:54,644
Oh.

653
00:56:02,276 --> 00:56:03,277
JEAN GREY: Logan...

654
00:56:05,238 --> 00:56:06,239
You're slipping.

655
00:56:06,322 --> 00:56:07,323
(GRUNTS)

656
00:56:07,949 --> 00:56:10,076
(SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

657
00:56:12,286 --> 00:56:13,287
(GROANS)

658
00:56:18,751 --> 00:56:20,336
(ZAPPING)
(GASPS)

659
00:56:20,419 --> 00:56:21,420
(LAUGHING)

660
00:56:22,755 --> 00:56:24,090
(GROANS)

661
00:56:24,882 --> 00:56:25,967
(SHOUTS IN JAPANESE)

662
00:56:26,968 --> 00:56:27,969
(GRUNTS)

663
00:56:28,636 --> 00:56:29,637
JEAN GREY: Logan...

664
00:56:31,055 --> 00:56:32,348
(TASER CRACKLING)

665
00:56:35,226 --> 00:56:36,227
(MAN 1 SPEAKING JAPANESE)

666
00:56:36,310 --> 00:56:37,562
Kill him already!

667
00:56:37,812 --> 00:56:40,690
Wanna say something
before you die, <i>gaijin?</i>

668
00:56:41,774 --> 00:56:43,401
(MAN 2 SCREAMS)

669
00:56:43,484 --> 00:56:45,278
(MAN 1 SPEAKING JAPANESE)

670
00:56:53,828 --> 00:56:54,829
(GRUNTS)

671
00:57:01,210 --> 00:57:03,004
(ZAPPING)
(EXCLAIMING IN PAIN)

672
00:57:04,046 --> 00:57:05,381
(GROANING)

673
00:57:09,844 --> 00:57:11,596
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

674
00:57:26,652 --> 00:57:27,903
(GOAT BLEATING)

675
00:57:28,321 --> 00:57:29,697
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

676
00:57:35,911 --> 00:57:37,872
(PEOPLE WHISPERING
IN JAPANESE)

677
00:57:43,711 --> 00:57:45,046
(MAN SHUSHING)

678
00:57:48,883 --> 00:57:50,301
(BULLETS CLATTERING)

679
00:57:58,601 --> 00:57:59,602
(SPEAKS JAPANESE)

680
00:58:04,148 --> 00:58:05,358
(GRUNTS)

681
00:58:08,069 --> 00:58:12,615
This is Mieko from the hotel
and her grandson, Hitoshi.

682
00:58:12,698 --> 00:58:14,617
Is he a doctor?

683
00:58:14,950 --> 00:58:17,453
In a manner
of speaking, yes.

684
00:58:17,620 --> 00:58:20,373
He's a veterinarian...

685
00:58:20,790 --> 00:58:22,416
student.

686
00:58:23,084 --> 00:58:24,710
Large animal.

687
00:58:24,794 --> 00:58:26,128
(BIRD CHIRPING)

688
00:58:29,423 --> 00:58:31,467
Uh... Thanks.
(GASPS)

689
00:58:31,550 --> 00:58:33,260
(INSTRUMENTS CLATTERING)
Whoa.

690
00:58:34,387 --> 00:58:37,932
You may have cut him
once or twice while
he was stitching you.

691
00:58:38,516 --> 00:58:41,352
Okay, okay, okay.

692
00:58:42,061 --> 00:58:43,479
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

693
00:58:51,028 --> 00:58:52,113
Hey.

694
00:58:53,781 --> 00:58:55,282
Thank you.

695
00:59:00,579 --> 00:59:01,622
I never needed
this before.

696
00:59:02,998 --> 00:59:04,917
What? Help?

697
00:59:10,631 --> 00:59:14,135
That doctor,
the one who helped your
grandfather, the blonde.

698
00:59:14,301 --> 00:59:15,261
Who is she?

699
00:59:15,344 --> 00:59:19,056
He met her last year
when he was in America
for treatment.

700
00:59:20,015 --> 00:59:23,227
Your grandfather
told me my healing
could be taken from me,

701
00:59:23,310 --> 00:59:24,311
passed on.

702
00:59:26,021 --> 00:59:28,899
I'm not getting better,
not like before.

703
00:59:30,151 --> 00:59:31,944
She did this to me.

704
00:59:42,872 --> 00:59:43,914
MAN: Blondie!

705
00:59:43,998 --> 00:59:45,040
(MAN SPEAKING JAPANESE)

706
00:59:45,207 --> 00:59:46,208
Blondie!

707
00:59:50,838 --> 00:59:53,841
How much?
How much, yeah?
How much?

708
01:00:00,014 --> 01:00:01,432
(PEOPLE GASPING)

709
01:00:14,069 --> 01:00:17,448
You kept me
waiting two hours.
You have no respect.

710
01:00:17,573 --> 01:00:19,074
So you haven't
found them?

711
01:00:22,953 --> 01:00:25,206
Don't play with me, bitch.
I could kill you.

712
01:00:25,414 --> 01:00:29,293
If you could make me
feel something, Harada,
that would be sublime.

713
01:00:29,543 --> 01:00:31,170
I can slit your
pretty mouth open,

714
01:00:31,253 --> 01:00:33,214
before you open it to
say one more stupid...

715
01:00:35,090 --> 01:00:36,383
Ah...

716
01:00:37,718 --> 01:00:40,513
I asked you to do
one thing, little man.

717
01:00:41,138 --> 01:00:42,765
Bring me the mutant.

718
01:00:42,848 --> 01:00:45,267
I don't work for you.
I work for the House of...

719
01:00:45,601 --> 01:00:47,269
(BLOWING AIR)
(GASPING)

720
01:00:48,062 --> 01:00:50,606
You work for Yashida,
I get it.

721
01:00:52,525 --> 01:00:55,361
Yet you cannot
fulfill his dying wish.

722
01:00:56,237 --> 01:00:59,323
My God, if you had
any idea how much
you have failed him.

723
01:00:59,907 --> 01:01:02,785
Where is Logan?
I am not done with him.

724
01:01:06,622 --> 01:01:08,165
(GASPING)

725
01:01:08,916 --> 01:01:10,793
The mutant has powers.

726
01:01:11,043 --> 01:01:12,253
(GRUNTS)

727
01:01:12,461 --> 01:01:16,298
He's just a man now.
His flesh is weak now.

728
01:01:16,590 --> 01:01:18,050
I did that.

729
01:01:18,342 --> 01:01:20,928
I suppressed his power
so he could be taken.

730
01:01:21,095 --> 01:01:23,973
You see, it's me
you should respect.

731
01:01:25,391 --> 01:01:26,433
(GRUNTS)

732
01:01:27,601 --> 01:01:30,396
Just find them,
before the Yakuza.

733
01:01:37,278 --> 01:01:38,779
(MUTTERING)

734
01:01:45,160 --> 01:01:46,245
(GRUNTS)

735
01:01:58,966 --> 01:02:00,885
We get off here.

736
01:02:19,987 --> 01:02:21,822
Where are we?

737
01:02:22,740 --> 01:02:24,533
Just outside Nagasaki.

738
01:02:33,667 --> 01:02:35,085
This way.

739
01:02:53,228 --> 01:02:55,606
This is the guy from
the funeral, the archer.

740
01:02:57,066 --> 01:02:58,901
He was your boyfriend.

741
01:02:59,068 --> 01:03:01,195
That's Harada.

742
01:03:02,529 --> 01:03:04,365
We were village
champions that summer.

743
01:03:05,407 --> 01:03:09,411
He with the bow
and me with the knives.

744
01:03:15,125 --> 01:03:17,628
Harada and I were
planning to get married.

745
01:03:17,795 --> 01:03:19,380
What stopped you?

746
01:03:19,546 --> 01:03:20,839
Grandfather.

747
01:03:21,006 --> 01:03:23,676
He said we had to wait
until we were at least 15.

748
01:03:31,225 --> 01:03:34,186
From the mountain,
from the sea.

749
01:03:35,562 --> 01:03:37,523
(BOTH SPEAKING JAPANESE)

750
01:03:40,067 --> 01:03:41,360
(SIGHS)

751
01:03:46,198 --> 01:03:49,034
Chopsticks upright
are a bad omen.

752
01:03:49,994 --> 01:03:52,079
It resembles incense
at a funeral.

753
01:03:55,582 --> 01:03:58,043
Nothing is without meaning.

754
01:03:59,503 --> 01:04:01,130
So, the other night
at the house,

755
01:04:01,213 --> 01:04:03,590
when you ran out
in the rain...

756
01:04:03,757 --> 01:04:05,926
what did that mean?

757
01:04:07,553 --> 01:04:09,680
My grandfather was dying.

758
01:04:10,556 --> 01:04:12,349
You knew he was gonna die.

759
01:04:12,433 --> 01:04:13,517
He'd been sick
for a long time.

760
01:04:13,684 --> 01:04:16,186
It wasn't
his death I feared.

761
01:04:16,770 --> 01:04:18,605
So, what, then?

762
01:04:20,899 --> 01:04:22,776
What did he tell
you that night?

763
01:04:26,280 --> 01:04:28,699
Mariko, why did
your father hit you?

764
01:04:29,783 --> 01:04:31,285
I was trying
to warn him.

765
01:04:31,452 --> 01:04:33,120
About what?

766
01:04:34,621 --> 01:04:36,957
What did your
grandfather tell you?

767
01:04:39,043 --> 01:04:42,254
He told me that...

768
01:04:43,922 --> 01:04:48,802
in three days,
when they read
his will...

769
01:04:51,138 --> 01:04:55,476
I will become
the most powerful
person in Japan.

770
01:04:58,312 --> 01:05:00,064
He gave it all to me.

771
01:05:01,732 --> 01:05:02,900
The company?

772
01:05:07,154 --> 01:05:09,156
I didn't want it.

773
01:05:11,241 --> 01:05:13,327
He knew that.

774
01:05:14,495 --> 01:05:17,247
I don't understand
why he gave it to me.

775
01:05:17,748 --> 01:05:20,000
It was all my father
dreamed of.

776
01:05:21,168 --> 01:05:23,003
Well, that's why.

777
01:05:27,257 --> 01:05:29,676
What about this
fiancé of yours?
Nostromo.

778
01:05:30,594 --> 01:05:31,845
Noburo.

779
01:05:32,012 --> 01:05:33,639
Does he know
about this?

780
01:05:33,806 --> 01:05:35,140
No.

781
01:05:36,517 --> 01:05:38,310
Why are you
marrying him?

782
01:05:38,685 --> 01:05:40,771
He seems like
kind of an asshole.

783
01:05:42,648 --> 01:05:44,983
My father arranged it
last year.

784
01:05:45,484 --> 01:05:46,527
What?

785
01:05:46,693 --> 01:05:49,863
It gives him a better access
to the political theater.

786
01:05:53,367 --> 01:05:56,620
To disobey my father
would be to dishonor him.

787
01:06:01,500 --> 01:06:03,919
I don't expect
you to understand.

788
01:06:06,630 --> 01:06:08,966
You're not Japanese.

789
01:06:14,054 --> 01:06:15,222
(SHINGEN SPEAKING JAPANESE)

790
01:06:15,305 --> 01:06:19,268
Our island is long and thin.

791
01:06:19,726 --> 01:06:21,895
Trains only run in two directions.

792
01:06:22,563 --> 01:06:23,939
I assure you Lord Shingen...

793
01:06:24,106 --> 01:06:25,983
my officers are making every effort...

794
01:06:26,150 --> 01:06:28,026
Then they're idiots.

795
01:06:28,235 --> 01:06:30,154
You've wasted enough of my time.

796
01:06:30,988 --> 01:06:33,073
I have my father's affairs to attend to.

797
01:06:35,742 --> 01:06:37,161
Get out and find her!

798
01:06:42,875 --> 01:06:46,086
Tell me you have
more promising news
from your contacts.

799
01:06:46,837 --> 01:06:48,797
They open the will
in three days.

800
01:06:49,298 --> 01:06:51,091
We are running
out of time.

801
01:06:52,384 --> 01:06:54,553
Soon, I hope.

802
01:06:55,179 --> 01:06:56,889
I'm sending men
to the South.

803
01:06:57,055 --> 01:06:59,099
That's where
we found the bodies.

804
01:07:08,817 --> 01:07:09,943
(YUKIO SPEAKING
JAPANESE ON PHONE)

805
01:07:10,027 --> 01:07:11,945
If the Yakuza got into the funeral...

806
01:07:12,279 --> 01:07:13,530
they had someone inside.

807
01:07:13,947 --> 01:07:16,200
They'll never find me here.

808
01:07:17,784 --> 01:07:19,036
You're not safe.

809
01:07:20,495 --> 01:07:21,955
I'm coming down there.

810
01:07:22,456 --> 01:07:23,624
They'll follow you.

811
01:07:23,957 --> 01:07:25,125
Please.

812
01:07:25,292 --> 01:07:27,878
Wait a few days.

813
01:07:28,128 --> 01:07:29,379
Please. I'm fine.

814
01:07:29,838 --> 01:07:31,298
Logan's here.

815
01:07:31,506 --> 01:07:33,467
He's wounded, Mariko.

816
01:07:33,550 --> 01:07:34,927
(WOMAN SPEAKING JAPANESE)

817
01:07:35,302 --> 01:07:36,303
Someone's here.

818
01:07:36,386 --> 01:07:37,095
LOGAN: Mariko?

819
01:07:37,137 --> 01:07:38,055
I have to go.

820
01:07:38,222 --> 01:07:39,389
Mariko?

821
01:07:40,599 --> 01:07:42,351
(WOMAN SPEAKING JAPANESE)

822
01:07:42,809 --> 01:07:45,437
A tree fell on the road.

823
01:07:45,812 --> 01:07:48,649
The men could use some help.

824
01:07:51,318 --> 01:07:53,320
(ALL SPEAKING JAPANESE)

825
01:08:08,043 --> 01:08:09,253
(GRUNTING)

826
01:08:19,680 --> 01:08:20,806
(EXHALES)

827
01:08:20,889 --> 01:08:22,516
Are you okay?

828
01:08:26,228 --> 01:08:27,229
Tired.

829
01:08:27,854 --> 01:08:29,523
Do you need something?

830
01:08:31,733 --> 01:08:32,734
No.

831
01:08:36,154 --> 01:08:37,739
(BOTH GREETING IN JAPANESE)

832
01:08:41,827 --> 01:08:42,953
This will help.

833
01:09:26,455 --> 01:09:28,248
(AIRPLANE APPROACHING)

834
01:09:34,588 --> 01:09:36,256
It's time.

835
01:09:39,134 --> 01:09:40,135
What?

836
01:09:41,178 --> 01:09:43,889
Please. Take it.

837
01:09:45,390 --> 01:09:46,933
Thank you.

838
01:10:05,285 --> 01:10:06,620
No.

839
01:10:08,288 --> 01:10:09,790
Two hands.

840
01:10:10,290 --> 01:10:14,127
Japanese sword
require two hands.

841
01:10:18,882 --> 01:10:21,051
Like that?
That's it.

842
01:10:23,678 --> 01:10:25,639
It's beautiful,
Yashida.

843
01:10:28,558 --> 01:10:29,810
But I can't take it.

844
01:10:30,310 --> 01:10:31,561
Please.

845
01:10:32,646 --> 01:10:33,980
Thank you.

846
01:10:40,362 --> 01:10:41,530
Keep it safe.

847
01:10:44,491 --> 01:10:46,326
Keep it safe for me.

848
01:10:48,912 --> 01:10:51,498
Someday,
I'll come get it.

849
01:10:59,172 --> 01:11:01,007
It's time.

850
01:11:21,153 --> 01:11:22,446
(GASPING)

851
01:11:38,211 --> 01:11:39,463
(SOBBING)

852
01:11:47,721 --> 01:11:51,349
I was here
when it happened.

853
01:11:53,852 --> 01:11:56,229
It's how I met
your grandfather.

854
01:11:56,605 --> 01:11:58,690
We hid in there.

855
01:12:00,275 --> 01:12:01,735
I heard the stories.

856
01:12:06,406 --> 01:12:08,033
My grandfather would say...

857
01:12:08,200 --> 01:12:11,369
what happened here
was proof that everything
in the world finds peace.

858
01:12:16,082 --> 01:12:18,084
Eventually.

859
01:12:22,422 --> 01:12:24,925
That man can
recover from anything.

860
01:12:28,970 --> 01:12:31,473
Maybe you, too.

861
01:12:37,395 --> 01:12:39,606
You don't sleep very well.

862
01:12:39,773 --> 01:12:41,733
You call out
in the night.

863
01:12:48,323 --> 01:12:49,616
Who's Jean?

864
01:13:04,631 --> 01:13:07,342
We should go back.
There's rain coming.

865
01:13:10,470 --> 01:13:11,846
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

866
01:13:28,113 --> 01:13:29,656
I'll make tea.

867
01:13:37,789 --> 01:13:39,124
For you.

868
01:14:04,274 --> 01:14:05,400
(SIGHS)

869
01:14:15,076 --> 01:14:16,578
This isn't right.

870
01:14:30,216 --> 01:14:33,470
You need this tied
like a proper samurai.

871
01:14:37,474 --> 01:14:39,643
Your grandfather
called me a ronin.

872
01:14:41,061 --> 01:14:43,396
A samurai
without a master.

873
01:14:45,273 --> 01:14:48,443
He said
I was destined
to live forever...

874
01:14:49,569 --> 01:14:51,988
with no reason to live.

875
01:14:56,951 --> 01:14:58,495
Was he right?

876
01:14:59,746 --> 01:15:01,081
Yes.

877
01:15:06,252 --> 01:15:07,962
Still?

878
01:15:57,178 --> 01:15:58,179
Hey.

879
01:15:59,180 --> 01:16:00,724
What are you doing?

880
01:16:05,311 --> 01:16:07,814
This isn't going
to end well.

881
01:16:12,193 --> 01:16:14,195
Everyone you love dies.

882
01:16:17,657 --> 01:16:19,367
(BLADE UNSHEATHES)
(GRUNTS)

883
01:16:21,786 --> 01:16:22,871
(GASPS)

884
01:16:23,663 --> 01:16:25,081
(PANTING)

885
01:16:27,500 --> 01:16:28,501
(YELLS)

886
01:16:34,883 --> 01:16:36,885
<i>Kuzuri.</i>

887
01:16:39,012 --> 01:16:40,680
Do you know
what that means?

888
01:16:45,351 --> 01:16:47,187
An animal.

889
01:16:47,353 --> 01:16:52,609
A fierce creature
with long claws
and sharp teeth.

890
01:16:54,694 --> 01:16:56,738
It fears nothing.

891
01:16:58,531 --> 01:17:02,577
When I was a girl,
I had nightmares.

892
01:17:03,244 --> 01:17:05,622
I'd wake up and
run to my parents.

893
01:17:06,581 --> 01:17:09,292
My father
would get angry.

894
01:17:09,834 --> 01:17:11,211
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

895
01:17:13,713 --> 01:17:16,800
"Go back to sleep.
Face your fears."

896
01:17:18,259 --> 01:17:20,762
My grandfather
was different.

897
01:17:21,721 --> 01:17:25,475
He told me stories
about <i>Kuzuri,</i> his friend.

898
01:17:26,392 --> 01:17:29,437
Who he met at the bottom
of a well.

899
01:17:31,564 --> 01:17:36,069
He said the <i>Kuzuri</i>
was magical and
saved his life.

900
01:17:38,404 --> 01:17:43,743
He said <i>Kuzuri</i>
would protect me, too,
as I slept in my bed.

901
01:17:45,328 --> 01:17:46,913
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

902
01:17:52,961 --> 01:17:54,504
Who's Jean?

903
01:18:02,178 --> 01:18:03,680
Is she like you?

904
01:18:06,432 --> 01:18:08,434
What happened to her?

905
01:18:09,769 --> 01:18:11,646
She died.

906
01:18:18,361 --> 01:18:20,113
I killed her.

907
01:18:26,786 --> 01:18:28,705
Along with the <i>Kuzuri.</i>

908
01:19:10,121 --> 01:19:11,372
Logan.

909
01:19:25,720 --> 01:19:27,639
Mariko?

910
01:19:29,974 --> 01:19:30,975
MARIKO: Logan!

911
01:19:31,851 --> 01:19:33,186
(MAN SHOUTING)
Logan!

912
01:19:34,729 --> 01:19:35,855
Mariko?

913
01:19:36,522 --> 01:19:37,690
Mariko!

914
01:19:38,483 --> 01:19:40,401
MARIKO: No! Logan!

915
01:19:46,199 --> 01:19:47,367
No!

916
01:19:48,242 --> 01:19:49,243
Logan!

917
01:19:49,869 --> 01:19:50,912
No!

918
01:19:57,377 --> 01:19:58,544
(GRUNTS)

919
01:20:02,757 --> 01:20:03,758
Mariko!

920
01:20:07,553 --> 01:20:08,554
MARIKO: Logan!

921
01:20:10,223 --> 01:20:11,349
No!

922
01:20:13,685 --> 01:20:14,686
Logan!

923
01:20:15,770 --> 01:20:17,563
Mariko! Mariko!

924
01:20:17,730 --> 01:20:19,190
Logan!

925
01:20:21,234 --> 01:20:22,485
(GRUNTING)

926
01:20:39,627 --> 01:20:40,878
Where are they
taking her?

927
01:20:41,129 --> 01:20:42,797
Where are they
taking her?

928
01:20:42,964 --> 01:20:44,424
Where, you piece of shit?

929
01:20:46,342 --> 01:20:48,928
I no talk, <i>gaijin.</i>

930
01:20:49,595 --> 01:20:51,472
I never talk.

931
01:20:55,476 --> 01:20:56,769
(MAN GROANS)

932
01:20:57,937 --> 01:21:00,106
Who hired you?

933
01:21:11,117 --> 01:21:12,994
Uh-oh.

934
01:21:23,296 --> 01:21:24,964
Take me to Noburo.

935
01:21:25,798 --> 01:21:27,633
Logan...
Take me to him.

936
01:21:28,551 --> 01:21:29,802
I need to tell
you something.

937
01:21:29,969 --> 01:21:31,888
Do it. Now.

938
01:21:51,157 --> 01:21:53,076
You wait in the car.

939
01:21:53,576 --> 01:21:55,578
Logan.
What?

940
01:21:56,412 --> 01:21:58,331
I saw you die.

941
01:21:58,498 --> 01:21:59,999
What?

942
01:22:00,500 --> 01:22:02,251
I saw you die.

943
01:22:02,668 --> 01:22:04,670
When? Just now?

944
01:22:05,129 --> 01:22:06,839
A while ago.

945
01:22:07,006 --> 01:22:09,884
But it's not like
I get a complete picture.

946
01:22:10,051 --> 01:22:12,303
More like looking
through a keyhole.

947
01:22:13,888 --> 01:22:16,140
But I'm always right.

948
01:22:17,016 --> 01:22:20,353
All I can see
is one part of
a person's life...

949
01:22:20,978 --> 01:22:22,522
their death.

950
01:22:23,231 --> 01:22:25,483
And I saw yours.

951
01:22:28,653 --> 01:22:30,571
So, what did you see?

952
01:22:31,030 --> 01:22:35,368
I see you on your back.
There's blood everywhere.

953
01:22:37,370 --> 01:22:40,414
You're holding
your own heart
in your hand.

954
01:22:42,500 --> 01:22:44,502
It's not beating.

955
01:22:45,336 --> 01:22:46,546
I don't have time
for this shit.

956
01:22:46,921 --> 01:22:50,758
When I was five,
I knew how my own
parents would die.

957
01:22:53,094 --> 01:22:56,597
Then I watched it happen
from the back seat.

958
01:22:59,559 --> 01:23:00,726
Look at me.

959
01:23:03,855 --> 01:23:06,566
A lot of people
have tried to kill me,
and I'm still here.

960
01:23:07,024 --> 01:23:08,693
Yeah...

961
01:23:08,860 --> 01:23:11,362
but you're
different now,
aren't you?

962
01:23:12,113 --> 01:23:14,031
They can hurt you.

963
01:23:14,198 --> 01:23:16,200
They can kill you.

964
01:23:16,367 --> 01:23:18,369
Just wait in the car.

965
01:23:29,213 --> 01:23:31,215
I said, wait in the car.
You need backup.

966
01:23:31,382 --> 01:23:33,259
You're not safe,
not in your condition.

967
01:23:35,261 --> 01:23:37,597
Just think of me
as your bodyguard.

968
01:23:38,514 --> 01:23:39,557
(SIGHS)

969
01:23:43,394 --> 01:23:44,478
(SLOW MUSIC PLAYING)

970
01:23:44,562 --> 01:23:45,938
(NOBURO CHUCKLING)

971
01:23:46,606 --> 01:23:48,399
WOMAN: Sexy.
(NOBURO LAUGHS)

972
01:23:55,448 --> 01:23:57,408
NOBURO: Come on!
WOMAN: I'm coming.

973
01:23:57,742 --> 01:23:59,160
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

974
01:24:00,995 --> 01:24:02,455
(ALL LAUGHING)

975
01:24:05,875 --> 01:24:08,920
WOMAN: Okay, round four.
Here we go.

976
01:24:11,130 --> 01:24:12,548
(NOBURO SPEAKING JAPANESE)

977
01:24:22,058 --> 01:24:23,476
WOMAN: Drink for you,
my lady.

978
01:24:29,482 --> 01:24:30,983
(BOTH SHRIEKING)

979
01:24:31,484 --> 01:24:32,568
Get out.

980
01:24:34,195 --> 01:24:35,488
(MUSIC STOPS)

981
01:24:38,157 --> 01:24:39,909
Not you.

982
01:24:41,827 --> 01:24:42,995
Call me old-fashioned...

983
01:24:43,162 --> 01:24:44,705
but I thought
being engaged meant

984
01:24:44,789 --> 01:24:45,998
you were done
with this kind
of bullshit.

985
01:24:46,165 --> 01:24:47,541
I am the Minister
of Justice.

986
01:24:47,625 --> 01:24:48,918
Do you have any idea
what I could do to you?

987
01:24:49,085 --> 01:24:50,962
Really? You're gonna
try and talk tough,

988
01:24:51,045 --> 01:24:52,838
standing there in
your red underwear?

989
01:24:53,339 --> 01:24:54,423
You have ten words...

990
01:24:54,674 --> 01:24:56,968
ten words...

991
01:24:57,093 --> 01:25:01,472
to explain to me why you,
the Minister of Justice...

992
01:25:01,639 --> 01:25:04,475
would want your fiancé
killed by the Yakuza.

993
01:25:04,600 --> 01:25:06,143
And if I don't
like what you say,

994
01:25:06,227 --> 01:25:08,854
you are going through
that fucking window.

995
01:25:09,730 --> 01:25:11,816
You don't have
the faintest idea
what's going on...

996
01:25:11,899 --> 01:25:13,025
(GROANS)

997
01:25:14,610 --> 01:25:16,570
How many words was that?
Nine.

998
01:25:16,737 --> 01:25:19,365
Nine.
You have one word left.

999
01:25:22,368 --> 01:25:23,035
Really?
(GRUNTS)

1000
01:25:25,079 --> 01:25:26,580
Shingen. Shingen!

1001
01:25:28,624 --> 01:25:29,792
Keep going.

1002
01:25:31,919 --> 01:25:33,254
Since he got sick...

1003
01:25:33,421 --> 01:25:36,924
old man Yashida
spent billions
on doctors, healers.

1004
01:25:37,091 --> 01:25:39,885
Stockpiling adamantium
at his lab in the North...

1005
01:25:40,052 --> 01:25:42,388
secretly trying
to prolong his life.

1006
01:25:42,555 --> 01:25:45,725
He brought the company
to the edge of bankruptcy.

1007
01:25:45,891 --> 01:25:48,060
He was obsessed
with you.

1008
01:25:48,894 --> 01:25:50,229
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1009
01:25:50,604 --> 01:25:51,897
(GROANS)
English!

1010
01:25:52,440 --> 01:25:55,443
Shingen lied,
protected the old man...

1011
01:25:55,609 --> 01:25:58,821
concealed the debt
from stockholders
and the board.

1012
01:25:58,988 --> 01:26:01,407
He tried to be a good son
and thought he'd be rewarded.

1013
01:26:02,491 --> 01:26:04,577
And then the old man
left everything to
his granddaughter.

1014
01:26:04,744 --> 01:26:07,330
If Mariko got all that power,
she would dump his ass.

1015
01:26:07,413 --> 01:26:08,414
It's true.

1016
01:26:08,581 --> 01:26:11,667
Mariko would have
never gone through
with the wedding...

1017
01:26:11,834 --> 01:26:14,337
not once the will
was revealed.

1018
01:26:15,087 --> 01:26:16,255
She never took to me.

1019
01:26:16,672 --> 01:26:19,467
Oh, really?
A class act like you.

1020
01:26:20,176 --> 01:26:22,803
Shingen promised me
a fortune for my help.

1021
01:26:23,971 --> 01:26:27,600
So, you put a hit
on his daughter.
Is that it?

1022
01:26:28,684 --> 01:26:30,686
Political careers
don't last forever.

1023
01:26:31,354 --> 01:26:32,355
That's right.

1024
01:26:32,646 --> 01:26:34,482
Wait! Wait! No!

1025
01:26:34,648 --> 01:26:37,443
You wanted the truth.
I told you the truth!

1026
01:26:38,361 --> 01:26:40,112
I didn't like it.

1027
01:26:40,780 --> 01:26:42,114
Wow.

1028
01:26:43,991 --> 01:26:45,451
How did you know
there's a pool
down there?

1029
01:26:45,618 --> 01:26:46,952
I didn't.

1030
01:26:57,380 --> 01:26:58,381
(SPEAKS JAPANESE)

1031
01:27:03,302 --> 01:27:07,640
Did you know I studied biology in college?

1032
01:27:09,558 --> 01:27:11,018
Genetics.

1033
01:27:15,022 --> 01:27:17,483
There are genes that skip generations.

1034
01:27:17,983 --> 01:27:19,819
Recessive genes.

1035
01:27:22,613 --> 01:27:23,364
Eyes.

1036
01:27:23,364 --> 01:27:24,490
Eyes. Hair.

1037
01:27:25,866 --> 01:27:27,159
Talent.

1038
01:27:28,577 --> 01:27:29,995
Temperament.

1039
01:27:32,164 --> 01:27:35,376
Not every child gets the same.

1040
01:27:36,168 --> 01:27:38,295
My father saw little of himself in me.

1041
01:27:39,505 --> 01:27:41,006
But in you...

1042
01:27:41,382 --> 01:27:43,801
he faced a mirror.

1043
01:28:03,279 --> 01:28:04,864
How did you convince my father...

1044
01:28:05,030 --> 01:28:06,449
to award you control...

1045
01:28:06,657 --> 01:28:08,075
of Asia's largest corporation?

1046
01:28:08,534 --> 01:28:09,994
You've gone insane.

1047
01:28:11,537 --> 01:28:13,372
I'm just waking up.

1048
01:28:15,082 --> 01:28:16,667
If you kill me, you will lose...

1049
01:28:16,876 --> 01:28:18,711
what little honor you have left.

1050
01:28:22,548 --> 01:28:23,716
Fear not Mariko.

1051
01:28:23,966 --> 01:28:26,260
I don't want to hurt you.

1052
01:28:26,719 --> 01:28:27,845
I want to help you.

1053
01:28:28,053 --> 01:28:29,722
Help you end your pain...

1054
01:28:29,930 --> 01:28:31,182
what that mutant stopped you...

1055
01:28:31,390 --> 01:28:32,600
from doing last week.

1056
01:28:32,892 --> 01:28:35,060
I never wanted to die, Father.

1057
01:28:43,569 --> 01:28:44,570
(GASPS)

1058
01:28:47,448 --> 01:28:48,824
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1059
01:28:51,368 --> 01:28:52,495
(HARADA SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1060
01:28:52,578 --> 01:28:53,871
It's alright, Mariko.

1061
01:28:53,996 --> 01:28:55,206
(GASPING)

1062
01:28:59,084 --> 01:28:59,793
Come with me.

1063
01:28:59,960 --> 01:29:00,794
What is happening?!

1064
01:29:01,128 --> 01:29:03,297
More than you can imagine.

1065
01:29:11,472 --> 01:29:13,265
You.

1066
01:29:13,682 --> 01:29:15,100
Me.

1067
01:29:15,267 --> 01:29:19,021
Sorry to interrupt,
but I need your
daughter alive.

1068
01:29:19,188 --> 01:29:20,523
What are you?

1069
01:29:21,357 --> 01:29:23,776
A chemist, a nihilist...

1070
01:29:24,193 --> 01:29:27,613
a capitalist,
a mutation.

1071
01:29:31,242 --> 01:29:32,743
A viper.

1072
01:29:34,328 --> 01:29:35,454
(CHOKES)

1073
01:29:36,997 --> 01:29:38,457
(GROANS)

1074
01:29:46,298 --> 01:29:47,299
(YELLS)

1075
01:30:02,982 --> 01:30:04,817
Where is
the security?

1076
01:30:24,837 --> 01:30:25,838
Yakuza.

1077
01:30:28,465 --> 01:30:29,466
Shingen?

1078
01:30:41,645 --> 01:30:42,896
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1079
01:30:50,070 --> 01:30:51,363
Logan.

1080
01:31:01,999 --> 01:31:03,542
This. This here.

1081
01:31:03,709 --> 01:31:05,336
Where is this?

1082
01:31:08,547 --> 01:31:10,549
Master Yashida's
birthplace.

1083
01:31:11,550 --> 01:31:14,386
The company
built a facility
into the mountainside.

1084
01:31:18,098 --> 01:31:19,391
How far?

1085
01:31:20,059 --> 01:31:22,645
500 kilometers from here.

1086
01:31:35,949 --> 01:31:36,992
(BEEPS)

1087
01:31:43,457 --> 01:31:44,792
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1088
01:31:57,096 --> 01:31:58,263
(GRUNTS)

1089
01:32:00,766 --> 01:32:02,017
(ELECTRONIC WHIRRING)

1090
01:32:29,586 --> 01:32:31,880
I gotta get that
thing out of me.

1091
01:32:32,339 --> 01:32:33,340
How?

1092
01:32:33,757 --> 01:32:34,883
No, stop, Logan.

1093
01:32:35,050 --> 01:32:38,053
I saw you die.
I'm never wrong.

1094
01:32:38,220 --> 01:32:40,264
I'm never wrong.
You're not always right.

1095
01:32:40,431 --> 01:32:41,640
You didn't know
the old man was
gonna bite it.

1096
01:32:41,807 --> 01:32:43,684
I saw you die in a room
like this with your heart
in your hand.

1097
01:32:43,851 --> 01:32:45,728
I can't leave her with
those freaks and killers.

1098
01:32:46,019 --> 01:32:49,314
I'm the only chance
she's got, but not with
that thing inside me.

1099
01:32:49,481 --> 01:32:50,733
You're going to die, Logan.

1100
01:32:50,816 --> 01:32:52,317
Maybe that's okay.
(GROANS)

1101
01:32:52,609 --> 01:32:54,445
No, listen to me, Logan!

1102
01:32:54,611 --> 01:32:56,613
No, stop. Logan!

1103
01:32:57,698 --> 01:32:59,116
You're not gonna want
to watch this part.
(GROANING)

1104
01:32:59,283 --> 01:33:01,744
No! Listen to me!
Please, no!

1105
01:33:02,453 --> 01:33:04,997
No, stop.
Listen to me.

1106
01:33:06,206 --> 01:33:07,291
Logan!

1107
01:33:13,672 --> 01:33:14,715
(SNIGGERS)

1108
01:33:16,049 --> 01:33:17,134
Move!
(YELLS)

1109
01:33:17,301 --> 01:33:18,761
Stay away from him.

1110
01:33:18,844 --> 01:33:20,095
(LOGAN SCREAMING)

1111
01:33:20,179 --> 01:33:21,972
He killed your master.

1112
01:33:22,598 --> 01:33:25,350
Put hands on your sister.

1113
01:33:25,601 --> 01:33:27,436
And now you want him?

1114
01:33:27,519 --> 01:33:29,021
(ALARM BLARING)

1115
01:33:30,189 --> 01:33:32,024
Oh, no. I can't see.

1116
01:33:32,941 --> 01:33:34,860
You'll always
be a beggar.

1117
01:33:34,985 --> 01:33:35,986
You're crazy.

1118
01:33:44,328 --> 01:33:45,370
LOGAN: Oh, no.

1119
01:33:46,622 --> 01:33:47,790
(BOTH GRUNT)

1120
01:33:52,753 --> 01:33:54,463
(GROANING)

1121
01:34:00,385 --> 01:34:01,553
(GASPING)

1122
01:34:02,971 --> 01:34:04,181
(GRUNTING)

1123
01:34:11,980 --> 01:34:13,232
(BEEPING)

1124
01:34:16,568 --> 01:34:17,820
Yukio.

1125
01:34:22,658 --> 01:34:23,992
(GROANING)

1126
01:34:25,786 --> 01:34:27,079
(EXHALES)

1127
01:34:31,792 --> 01:34:33,502
(HEART MONITOR FLATLINING)

1128
01:34:37,339 --> 01:34:38,423
Logan!

1129
01:34:39,216 --> 01:34:40,509
(YUKIO YELLING)

1130
01:34:45,514 --> 01:34:47,724
Logan! Logan!

1131
01:34:48,600 --> 01:34:49,685
Logan!

1132
01:35:32,019 --> 01:35:34,021
Don't hit my friends.

1133
01:35:37,107 --> 01:35:38,191
Where's Mariko?

1134
01:35:38,358 --> 01:35:41,153
She's gone.
That Viper bitch
took her.

1135
01:35:41,320 --> 01:35:43,697
It was my father's
obsession...

1136
01:35:44,406 --> 01:35:47,159
with mutation,
with God's mistakes...

1137
01:35:48,702 --> 01:35:52,873
like you and her,
that ruined this house.

1138
01:35:54,833 --> 01:35:56,293
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1139
01:37:05,862 --> 01:37:07,531
You tried to kill
your daughter.

1140
01:37:10,200 --> 01:37:11,660
Live with that.

1141
01:37:20,002 --> 01:37:21,211
(YELLING)

1142
01:37:26,842 --> 01:37:29,636
What kind
of monster are you?

1143
01:37:30,512 --> 01:37:32,097
The Wolverine.

1144
01:37:45,402 --> 01:37:48,447
Hey, come here,
come here. That's it.

1145
01:37:49,114 --> 01:37:50,115
I was wrong.

1146
01:37:50,741 --> 01:37:52,159
I told you.

1147
01:37:52,325 --> 01:37:54,077
Let me have
a look at you.

1148
01:37:54,953 --> 01:37:56,413
It's nothing.

1149
01:37:56,580 --> 01:37:59,249
Hey, thank you.

1150
01:38:11,470 --> 01:38:13,764
It's a trap, Logan.

1151
01:38:32,324 --> 01:38:32,949
(MARIKO SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1152
01:38:32,991 --> 01:38:35,077
Why have you brought me here?

1153
01:38:35,660 --> 01:38:36,995
What are you hiding?

1154
01:38:37,329 --> 01:38:38,914
You will soon find out.

1155
01:38:40,999 --> 01:38:43,126
Welcome, Mariko.

1156
01:38:44,294 --> 01:38:47,464
It's all right, Mariko.
She also serves
the House of Yashida.

1157
01:38:47,631 --> 01:38:49,007
MARIKO:
She serves herself.

1158
01:38:49,174 --> 01:38:51,468
She infected Logan.

1159
01:38:51,802 --> 01:38:52,928
Hmm...

1160
01:38:53,178 --> 01:38:54,346
And what about
Grandfather?

1161
01:38:55,305 --> 01:38:56,932
What did you
infect him with?

1162
01:38:59,768 --> 01:39:02,145
I granted
his dying wish.

1163
01:39:02,771 --> 01:39:04,856
I helped him rest.

1164
01:39:06,983 --> 01:39:09,319
Now, it's your turn.

1165
01:39:12,197 --> 01:39:13,365
(GASPS)

1166
01:39:17,869 --> 01:39:19,037
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1167
01:39:43,103 --> 01:39:45,897
Listen to me, mutant.
She will not be harmed.

1168
01:39:47,357 --> 01:39:48,942
She will be fine.

1169
01:39:50,068 --> 01:39:52,237
So long as you do your job.

1170
01:39:53,196 --> 01:39:56,074
Logan will be here soon,
you should prepare.

1171
01:39:56,616 --> 01:39:58,869
It was easy
to lure him here.

1172
01:39:59,244 --> 01:40:00,704
It's another thing
to capture him.

1173
01:40:00,787 --> 01:40:03,874
We're ready.
He's never faced
the Black Clan.

1174
01:40:06,585 --> 01:40:07,794
Yes, well...

1175
01:40:09,796 --> 01:40:11,965
Dip your arrows in this.

1176
01:40:12,674 --> 01:40:14,384
It won't kill him,

1177
01:40:15,051 --> 01:40:16,970
but it will slow him down.

1178
01:40:17,053 --> 01:40:18,180
Keep your potions.

1179
01:40:18,513 --> 01:40:20,932
He's no challenge
for us now. He's weak.

1180
01:40:21,808 --> 01:40:22,893
Okay.

1181
01:40:26,188 --> 01:40:27,939
But when you fail...

1182
01:40:29,399 --> 01:40:30,817
you have this.

1183
01:40:48,376 --> 01:40:50,295
VIPER: Did you have
a nice rest?

1184
01:40:57,510 --> 01:40:58,762
I don't know
what you said or did

1185
01:40:58,845 --> 01:41:00,180
to deceive Harada
or my grandfather...

1186
01:41:00,347 --> 01:41:01,806
Now, now, calm down.

1187
01:41:01,973 --> 01:41:03,975
Your grandfather
sought me out.

1188
01:41:04,351 --> 01:41:06,144
I am the head
of this family now.

1189
01:41:10,398 --> 01:41:12,984
And why do you
suppose that is?

1190
01:41:14,819 --> 01:41:17,781
Why do you think
the old man chose you?

1191
01:41:21,034 --> 01:41:22,744
Because you are strong?

1192
01:41:23,703 --> 01:41:25,830
Or because you are weak?

1193
01:42:20,969 --> 01:42:22,679
I see you've
come to fight.

1194
01:42:22,846 --> 01:42:24,014
It's pointless.

1195
01:42:24,180 --> 01:42:26,516
You're weak.
You're outnumbered.

1196
01:42:26,683 --> 01:42:30,645
The Black Clan
has protected the House
of Yashida for 700 years.

1197
01:42:32,105 --> 01:42:33,732
Is that all the men
you brought?

1198
01:42:37,068 --> 01:42:38,695
I'm gonna get her.

1199
01:42:39,279 --> 01:42:41,281
We are grateful
for your protection
of Mariko.

1200
01:42:41,448 --> 01:42:44,576
But there is one more
sacrifice you must
make for her family.

1201
01:42:45,869 --> 01:42:47,996
Go fuck yourself,
pretty boy.

1202
01:42:49,539 --> 01:42:50,999
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1203
01:42:56,296 --> 01:42:57,547
(SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

1204
01:42:57,630 --> 01:42:58,840
(MEN SHOUTING)

1205
01:43:23,448 --> 01:43:25,283
(SHOUTING IN JAPANESE)

1206
01:44:17,669 --> 01:44:18,837
(STARTS ENGINE)

1207
01:44:38,565 --> 01:44:39,899
(GRUNTS)

1208
01:44:42,527 --> 01:44:43,528
(SCREAMS)

1209
01:45:38,583 --> 01:45:39,834
(PANTING)

1210
01:45:50,011 --> 01:45:51,012
Yukio, run!

1211
01:45:58,436 --> 01:45:59,604
(SPITS)

1212
01:46:01,940 --> 01:46:02,941
(YELLS)

1213
01:46:05,193 --> 01:46:06,611
(NINJAS SCREAMING)

1214
01:46:42,146 --> 01:46:43,356
(GROANING)

1215
01:46:52,907 --> 01:46:54,409
(MEN SHOUTING)

1216
01:47:03,167 --> 01:47:04,460
Logan.

1217
01:47:05,253 --> 01:47:06,671
(GROANING)

1218
01:47:21,227 --> 01:47:22,437
(GROANS)

1219
01:48:36,844 --> 01:48:38,262
KAYLA: <i>Logan.</i>

1220
01:48:38,388 --> 01:48:39,430
LOGAN: <i>Kayla.</i>

1221
01:48:39,555 --> 01:48:40,723
<i>I love you.
Kayla!</i>

1222
01:48:40,848 --> 01:48:42,183
<i>Logan.</i>
(LOGAN GROANS)

1223
01:48:47,146 --> 01:48:48,606
MARIKO: <i>Logan!</i>
LOGAN: <i>Mariko!</i>

1224
01:48:50,566 --> 01:48:51,567
Jean.

1225
01:48:52,610 --> 01:48:53,986
JEAN GREY: <i>Save me.</i>

1226
01:48:57,073 --> 01:48:58,449
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1227
01:49:09,961 --> 01:49:11,129
(GRUNTING)

1228
01:49:21,055 --> 01:49:22,140
(GRUNTS)

1229
01:49:22,765 --> 01:49:24,225
(PANTING)

1230
01:49:25,226 --> 01:49:27,186
Stand back.
There is no need.

1231
01:49:27,437 --> 01:49:29,313
Where is she?
Where's Mariko?

1232
01:49:29,439 --> 01:49:30,440
Where is she?

1233
01:49:31,357 --> 01:49:33,526
"Where is Mariko?"

1234
01:49:33,693 --> 01:49:35,945
Still pining away?

1235
01:49:36,112 --> 01:49:37,947
That's so sweet.

1236
01:49:39,073 --> 01:49:40,992
Impressive, no?

1237
01:49:41,242 --> 01:49:44,829
He is made of adamantium,
just like you.

1238
01:49:54,422 --> 01:49:55,423
(GRUNTS)

1239
01:49:55,506 --> 01:49:59,218
Oh, Logan,
you know what, I get it.
You're frustrated.

1240
01:49:59,385 --> 01:50:01,471
I know she's here.
I want to see her.

1241
01:50:02,513 --> 01:50:03,806
You want answers.

1242
01:50:04,849 --> 01:50:06,058
Yes, I want answers!

1243
01:50:06,225 --> 01:50:08,060
I'm sorry,
I wish I could say more,

1244
01:50:08,144 --> 01:50:10,021
but I was hired in
part for my discretion.

1245
01:50:10,188 --> 01:50:11,063
I'm sure you were.

1246
01:50:12,190 --> 01:50:13,399
That...

1247
01:50:13,566 --> 01:50:18,321
and a certain talent
for combining biochemistry
and metaphysics.

1248
01:50:18,863 --> 01:50:21,741
High-grade toxins
are my specialty.

1249
01:50:22,200 --> 01:50:24,368
It helps to be
genetically immune

1250
01:50:24,452 --> 01:50:26,871
to every poison
known to man, as I am.

1251
01:50:27,872 --> 01:50:31,876
And immune to the toxin
that is man himself...

1252
01:50:33,044 --> 01:50:34,378
as I am.

1253
01:50:34,879 --> 01:50:37,215
I'll tell you what,
you twisted mutant bitch...

1254
01:50:38,090 --> 01:50:39,634
why don't you
open these bracelets

1255
01:50:39,717 --> 01:50:41,677
and we'll see
who's made of what?

1256
01:50:44,764 --> 01:50:46,140
(GRUNTING)

1257
01:50:46,224 --> 01:50:48,893
The claws.
Now we can begin.

1258
01:50:48,976 --> 01:50:50,228
(GROANING)

1259
01:50:50,311 --> 01:50:51,479
(HARADA SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1260
01:50:51,562 --> 01:50:53,898
I know you care for him.

1261
01:50:54,315 --> 01:50:55,858
You need to let go of that.

1262
01:50:56,108 --> 01:50:58,152
You are a Yashida.

1263
01:50:58,402 --> 01:51:00,279
She betrayed my grandfather...

1264
01:51:00,780 --> 01:51:02,114
and so have you.

1265
01:51:02,740 --> 01:51:03,574
No Mariko.

1266
01:51:03,908 --> 01:51:05,743
We grew up together.

1267
01:51:05,993 --> 01:51:07,370
You need to trust me.

1268
01:51:08,579 --> 01:51:10,373
Let me go to him!

1269
01:51:10,581 --> 01:51:13,000
He saved my life!

1270
01:51:13,209 --> 01:51:15,586
Let him go, Mariko!

1271
01:51:15,920 --> 01:51:17,046
This isn't easy for me but...

1272
01:51:17,338 --> 01:51:20,216
I'm following Grandfather's wishes.

1273
01:51:20,299 --> 01:51:23,761
The suppressant bug
you found inside
of you was mine.

1274
01:51:24,095 --> 01:51:26,681
You took it out
on your own.

1275
01:51:27,682 --> 01:51:29,684
I didn't see that coming.

1276
01:51:30,101 --> 01:51:31,477
The Viper woman is evil...

1277
01:51:31,686 --> 01:51:33,437
we both know that.

1278
01:51:33,646 --> 01:51:36,440
But she's a means to an end...

1279
01:51:36,858 --> 01:51:37,859
LOGAN: (GRUNTS)
Where is she?

1280
01:51:37,942 --> 01:51:39,569
An end your grandfather wanted.

1281
01:51:39,652 --> 01:51:40,778
VIPER: You are strong.

1282
01:51:41,153 --> 01:51:42,780
You have courage.

1283
01:51:43,531 --> 01:51:44,866
Real courage.

1284
01:51:44,949 --> 01:51:46,367
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1285
01:51:48,536 --> 01:51:51,330
But that won't
help much now.

1286
01:52:04,635 --> 01:52:05,803
What the...?

1287
01:52:06,679 --> 01:52:08,306
You need to trust me.

1288
01:52:08,890 --> 01:52:10,182
Is that hard?

1289
01:52:10,892 --> 01:52:13,519
We were meant to be together.

1290
01:52:14,020 --> 01:52:16,022
We still can be.

1291
01:52:16,981 --> 01:52:18,441
Perhaps.

1292
01:52:26,574 --> 01:52:27,742
(GROANING)

1293
01:52:45,009 --> 01:52:46,218
(PANTING)

1294
01:52:47,219 --> 01:52:48,220
MARIKO: Stop!

1295
01:52:50,765 --> 01:52:52,350
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1296
01:52:54,352 --> 01:52:55,561
This is madness.

1297
01:53:01,192 --> 01:53:02,318
Let's go.

1298
01:53:05,237 --> 01:53:06,238
Go!

1299
01:53:07,323 --> 01:53:08,282
Run!

1300
01:53:08,366 --> 01:53:09,575
(SNARLING)

1301
01:53:09,659 --> 01:53:10,660
(CHOKES)

1302
01:53:21,712 --> 01:53:23,255
Come on.

1303
01:53:38,938 --> 01:53:40,314
Mariko, come!
Go! Run!

1304
01:53:43,234 --> 01:53:44,402
(GRUNTING)

1305
01:53:50,116 --> 01:53:51,450
(GROANING)

1306
01:53:59,625 --> 01:54:01,043
Mariko, get out!

1307
01:54:01,961 --> 01:54:03,170
(GRUNTING)

1308
01:54:14,390 --> 01:54:15,766
(SNARLS)

1309
01:54:18,185 --> 01:54:19,437
(GRUNTING)

1310
01:54:28,362 --> 01:54:29,613
(SCREAMING)

1311
01:54:49,300 --> 01:54:50,468
(GROANING)

1312
01:54:54,722 --> 01:54:55,848
(SCREAMS)

1313
01:55:07,318 --> 01:55:08,819
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1314
01:55:12,364 --> 01:55:13,449
Ahhh!

1315
01:55:16,494 --> 01:55:17,661
(GROANS)

1316
01:55:20,122 --> 01:55:21,373
(PANTING)

1317
01:55:23,459 --> 01:55:24,877
(GROANING)

1318
01:56:01,330 --> 01:56:02,456
(YELLING)

1319
01:56:33,654 --> 01:56:34,780
(GROANS)

1320
01:56:35,322 --> 01:56:36,657
(HARADA SHOUTING)

1321
01:56:49,920 --> 01:56:51,088
Come on.

1322
01:56:51,922 --> 01:56:53,090
This is not the way.

1323
01:56:55,176 --> 01:56:56,552
(GASPING)

1324
01:57:06,604 --> 01:57:08,105
Two hands.

1325
01:57:12,610 --> 01:57:13,736
Master...

1326
01:57:21,952 --> 01:57:24,121
Hey! Bub!

1327
01:57:29,793 --> 01:57:31,045
(GRUNTS)

1328
01:57:36,592 --> 01:57:37,676
(SCREAMS)

1329
01:57:38,719 --> 01:57:40,262
(GRUNTING)

1330
01:57:43,641 --> 01:57:44,642
MARIKO: Harada.

1331
01:57:50,147 --> 01:57:51,232
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1332
01:57:51,315 --> 01:57:52,816
I'm sorry.

1333
01:57:54,318 --> 01:57:55,736
(GASPING)

1334
01:58:02,284 --> 01:58:03,285
(LOGAN GRUNTING)

1335
01:58:13,420 --> 01:58:15,005
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1336
01:58:19,176 --> 01:58:20,386
(SCREAMING)

1337
01:58:37,194 --> 01:58:38,529
(YUKIO YELLING)

1338
01:58:41,198 --> 01:58:42,700
(BOTH PANTING)

1339
01:58:43,242 --> 01:58:44,285
Now, you die.

1340
01:58:45,035 --> 01:58:46,453
Today is not my day.

1341
01:58:54,878 --> 01:58:56,213
(CABLES WHIRRING)

1342
01:59:03,470 --> 01:59:04,555
(GROANING)

1343
01:59:12,062 --> 01:59:13,480
(YELLING)

1344
01:59:16,900 --> 01:59:18,152
(GRUNTING)

1345
01:59:25,159 --> 01:59:26,327
(GROANING)

1346
01:59:31,749 --> 01:59:33,083
Hey!

1347
01:59:40,257 --> 01:59:41,925
Logan-<i>san.</i>

1348
01:59:42,092 --> 01:59:44,094
Don't look so shocked.

1349
01:59:46,513 --> 01:59:50,351
With you at my side,
I survived Nagasaki.

1350
01:59:50,517 --> 01:59:53,103
Surely,
I could survive this.

1351
01:59:54,772 --> 01:59:57,608
It's all right.
It won't take long.

1352
01:59:58,192 --> 02:00:01,195
Dr. Green and I
have been waiting.
(GROANING LOUDLY)

1353
02:00:01,445 --> 02:00:05,032
It's only this armor
that's kept me alive.

1354
02:00:05,199 --> 02:00:10,120
We built it to make me
strong, so I can take
what you would not give.

1355
02:00:10,287 --> 02:00:13,457
And transfer your
unwanted healing...

1356
02:00:14,375 --> 02:00:16,543
to my body.

1357
02:00:18,837 --> 02:00:22,132
My legacy must
be preserved.

1358
02:00:22,800 --> 02:00:26,387
Your mistake was to believe
that a life without end...

1359
02:00:26,553 --> 02:00:27,846
can have no meaning.

1360
02:00:30,808 --> 02:00:33,644
It is the only
life that can.

1361
02:00:35,020 --> 02:00:36,522
Hold on.

1362
02:00:36,688 --> 02:00:38,482
We are almost there.

1363
02:00:38,649 --> 02:00:42,694
The peace,
the peace you've wanted.

1364
02:00:43,153 --> 02:00:45,322
Your reward.

1365
02:00:45,989 --> 02:00:49,159
You know,
I'm giving you
the very death...

1366
02:00:49,660 --> 02:00:51,870
you longed for.

1367
02:00:52,621 --> 02:00:53,914
(CHUCKLES)

1368
02:00:54,331 --> 02:00:55,499
(INHALES)

1369
02:01:04,675 --> 02:01:05,717
This feeling...

1370
02:01:06,885 --> 02:01:09,388
to be invincible...

1371
02:01:12,015 --> 02:01:13,725
like you.

1372
02:01:13,976 --> 02:01:15,269
(MARIKO GRUNTS)
(GASPS)

1373
02:01:25,028 --> 02:01:26,447
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1374
02:01:26,530 --> 02:01:28,699
You are a monster.

1375
02:01:29,158 --> 02:01:30,325
Mariko.

1376
02:01:31,034 --> 02:01:33,579
It's me.
Your grandfather.

1377
02:01:35,414 --> 02:01:36,999
I buried my grandfather.

1378
02:01:37,416 --> 02:01:38,667
(GROANS)

1379
02:01:55,267 --> 02:01:56,435
(PANTING)

1380
02:02:22,503 --> 02:02:23,712
(GRUNTING)

1381
02:02:24,963 --> 02:02:26,590
(ARMOR SHORT-CIRCUITING)

1382
02:02:27,925 --> 02:02:29,259
(YELLING)

1383
02:02:30,844 --> 02:02:32,012
(GROANS)

1384
02:02:40,145 --> 02:02:42,773
You asked me to
come say goodbye.

1385
02:02:43,440 --> 02:02:45,108
<i>Sayonara.</i>

1386
02:02:46,276 --> 02:02:47,277
(SCREAMING)

1387
02:02:48,445 --> 02:02:49,821
(CRASHING)

1388
02:02:58,288 --> 02:02:59,665
(PANTING)

1389
02:03:07,506 --> 02:03:09,341
Are you all right?

1390
02:03:18,642 --> 02:03:19,643
Logan.

1391
02:03:29,820 --> 02:03:31,697
JEAN GREY:
(WHISPERING) Logan.

1392
02:03:34,700 --> 02:03:35,867
Logan.

1393
02:03:48,005 --> 02:03:49,464
You're here.

1394
02:03:51,675 --> 02:03:53,385
Of course.

1395
02:03:55,053 --> 02:03:57,014
Can you stay?

1396
02:03:59,182 --> 02:04:01,184
I can't.

1397
02:04:03,562 --> 02:04:05,230
Yes, you can.

1398
02:04:07,024 --> 02:04:09,192
This is what you wanted.

1399
02:04:11,361 --> 02:04:12,696
Not anymore.

1400
02:04:17,659 --> 02:04:20,203
I'm all alone here.

1401
02:04:24,499 --> 02:04:26,543
You put me here.

1402
02:04:28,462 --> 02:04:30,881
You were hurting
people, Jean.

1403
02:04:32,174 --> 02:04:33,634
I had to.

1404
02:04:42,142 --> 02:04:44,311
I love you, Jean.

1405
02:04:49,858 --> 02:04:51,693
I always will.

1406
02:05:25,018 --> 02:05:26,353
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1407
02:05:28,355 --> 02:05:31,233
You are my only family.

1408
02:05:32,776 --> 02:05:35,112
Be well, sister.

1409
02:05:48,583 --> 02:05:51,795
Am I wrong to think
you might visit me soon?

1410
02:06:03,306 --> 02:06:04,641
Stay.

1411
02:06:06,309 --> 02:06:07,811
I can't, princess.

1412
02:06:08,729 --> 02:06:10,147
I'm a soldier,

1413
02:06:10,230 --> 02:06:11,982
and I've been
hiding too long.

1414
02:06:25,662 --> 02:06:28,331
MALE NEWS ANCHOR ON TV:
<i>In our business profile
tonight, Mariko Yashida.</i>

1415
02:06:28,498 --> 02:06:31,334
<i>A two-generation
passing of the torch
in the Yashida family...</i>

1416
02:06:31,501 --> 02:06:34,254
<i>as Mariko Yashida
takes the helm from
her grandfather,</i>

1417
02:06:34,337 --> 02:06:35,464
<i>who built this tech giant.</i>

1418
02:06:35,630 --> 02:06:37,716
MARIKO ON TV: <i>I know
it will always be the purpose</i>

1419
02:06:37,799 --> 02:06:39,843
<i>for a corporation
to make a profit...</i>

1420
02:06:40,010 --> 02:06:44,306
<i>but Yashida Industries
believes we can also work
with our community.</i>

1421
02:06:50,645 --> 02:06:52,856
So, have you decided?

1422
02:06:55,317 --> 02:06:56,318
What?

1423
02:06:56,777 --> 02:06:59,029
Mariko says we can
go wherever we want.

1424
02:06:59,196 --> 02:07:00,864
Just say where.

1425
02:07:02,157 --> 02:07:03,492
What are you doing?

1426
02:07:05,619 --> 02:07:07,370
I'm your bodyguard.

1427
02:07:12,000 --> 02:07:13,627
So, where do
you want to go?

1428
02:07:14,336 --> 02:07:15,545
(SIGHS)

1429
02:07:15,879 --> 02:07:16,922
Uh...

1430
02:07:17,464 --> 02:07:19,382
Let's just start with up.

1431
02:07:19,549 --> 02:07:21,218
And then?

1432
02:07:25,222 --> 02:07:26,890
We'll see.

1433
02:07:29,309 --> 02:07:30,560
Interesting.

1434
02:07:39,110 --> 02:07:40,403
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

1435
02:09:22,130 --> 02:09:24,257
FEMALE ANNOUNCER ON TV:
<i>With cutting edge technology,</i>

1436
02:09:24,341 --> 02:09:26,343
<i>and the world's
leading minds...</i>

1437
02:09:26,509 --> 02:09:28,094
<i>we are on the frontlines...</i>

1438
02:09:28,261 --> 02:09:31,473
<i>keeping you healthy,
keeping you safe.</i>

1439
02:09:31,932 --> 02:09:34,017
<i>Trask Industries.</i>

1440
02:09:34,184 --> 02:09:36,478
<i>Solving tomorrow's
problems, today.</i>

1441
02:09:37,354 --> 02:09:38,772
I'll take the pat-down.

1442
02:09:38,939 --> 02:09:39,940
Opt out.

1443
02:09:41,858 --> 02:09:43,193
(METAL RATTLING)

1444
02:09:50,951 --> 02:09:52,118
(MACHINE BEEPING)

1445
02:09:52,869 --> 02:09:54,037
GUARD: You can go ahead, sir.

1446
02:09:54,120 --> 02:09:55,205
MAN: I'll wait.

1447
02:09:57,582 --> 02:09:58,583
(STRAINING)

1448
02:10:03,838 --> 02:10:05,340
What do you want?

1449
02:10:07,050 --> 02:10:09,552
There are dark forces,
Wolverine.

1450
02:10:11,221 --> 02:10:13,348
Human forces
building a weapon...

1451
02:10:13,515 --> 02:10:16,935
that could bring about
the end of our kind.

1452
02:10:19,771 --> 02:10:22,899
What do I want?
I want your help.

1453
02:10:23,358 --> 02:10:24,943
Why would I trust you?

1454
02:10:26,111 --> 02:10:27,445
You wouldn't.

1455
02:10:28,196 --> 02:10:29,239
(GASPS)

1456
02:10:29,656 --> 02:10:30,824
(PANTING)

1457
02:10:52,095 --> 02:10:53,430
Hello, Logan.

1458
02:10:57,767 --> 02:10:59,602
How is this possible?

1459
02:10:59,769 --> 02:11:02,564
As I told you
a long time ago...

1460
02:11:03,815 --> 02:11:06,359
you are not
the only one with gifts.

1461
02:11:06,443 --> 02:11:07,569
(SIGHS)

